1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,097
Gosh, that's nice.

2
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:17,225
DAY BEFORE HIKE
YEONGNAM ALPS BASE CAMP

3
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:21,771
TARZZAN IS ON THE PHONE WITH SOMEONE

4
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:23,648
Hey, guys.

5
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:26,276
Bailey wants to say hi to you.

6
00:00:54,095 --> 00:00:54,929
<i>Cha.</i>

7
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,224
Jung-won.

8
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:03,521
SORRY FOR BEING SILLY

9
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:07,400
NEXT, HE INTRODUCES DOWOON

10
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:19,662
I'm telling her you're a drummer!

11
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:20,872
I'm a drummer.

12
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>Hello.</i>

13
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:26,795
And the one who's an actor
is in the bathroom.

14
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:31,883
THE SWEET BAILEY WISHES THEM
A SAFE HIKE TOMORROW

15
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:36,930
Let's plan the schedule quickly
before we shower.

16
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,056
Okay.

17
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:39,516
The Yeongnam Alps.

18
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,768
THE MEMBERS HAVE GATHERED
TO PLAN THE THIRD HIKE

19
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,645
Which mountains are we climbing again?

20
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:47,023
The mountains we'll attempt
to climb tomorrow are…

21
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:49,651
THE THIRD QUEST

22
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:52,987
<i>Three peaks of the Yeongnam Alps.</i>

23
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,908
OUT OF THE 9 PEAKS OF THE YEONGNAM ALPS

24
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,201
THE 1-DAY

25
00:01:58,284 --> 00:01:59,494
3-PEAK

26
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:01,162
CHALLENGE

27
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,207
DIFFICULTY: MODERATE

28
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,667
WALK THE RIDGE

29
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:06,709
WALK IT

30
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,962
AND KEEP WALKING IT

31
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,673
BAENAEGOGAE PARKING LOT, GANWOLSAN,
SINBULSAN, YEONGCHUKSAN

32
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:13,967
TOTAL HIKING DISTANCE OF ABOUT 16 KM

33
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,176
First off,

34
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,803
how long does it take to get there?

35
00:02:16,886 --> 00:02:18,138
About ten minutes.

36
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:19,430
-From here?
-Yes.

37
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:22,308
We'll be going to a place called
Baenaegogae Parking Lot.

38
00:02:22,392 --> 00:02:25,311
TAKES LESS THAN 10 MINUTES BY CAR
FROM BASE CAMP TO STARTING POINT

39
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:29,315
SCHEDULED TO START HIKING AT 8:00 A.M.

40
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,651
If we start at 8:00 a.m. to hike…

41
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:34,279
Then, should we put
wake-up time at 7:00 a.m.?

42
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:35,947
-At 7:00 a.m. and…
-Get up at 7:10 a.m.?

43
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,991
-You can wake up anytime.
-It's up to us?

44
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:40,827
But at 7:20 a.m.,
Lee Chae-min and Lee Chae-won will eat.

45
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,496
At 7:20 a.m., Chae and Chae will eat.

46
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:44,789
-Chae and Chae will eat.
-Okay.

47
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:46,708
Then, we'll leave at 7:45 a.m.

48
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:48,918
7:45 A.M.
LEAVE BASE CAMP

49
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:50,253
IN COMMAND

50
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,171
Sounds good.

51
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:53,214
This is important.
It'll get us up at 7:00 a.m.

52
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,465
-Exactly.
-"Depart."

53
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,759
You can brush teeth
and wash your face in five minutes.

54
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:59,178
At 8:00 a.m., we start climbing.

55
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:00,930
-"Climbing starts."
-That's right.

56
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,181
This is a pure Korean word.

57
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,600
You have nice handwriting.

58
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:04,517
CHUCKLING

59
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:05,894
8:00 A.M.
START CLIMBING

60
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:09,606
You said the first mountain
takes an hour to climb, right?

61
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:11,566
It takes about two hours to the peak.

62
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:12,483
GANWOLSAN

63
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,819
Two hours?
Then, we should arrive by 10:00 a.m.

64
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:17,739
If you walk down from Ganwolsan
for about 30 minutes,

65
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:21,117
there's a silver grass field
called Ganwoljae.

66
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,119
It has a rest area and a cafeteria there.

67
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:26,247
<i>They sell cup noodles.</i>
<i>You can eat them there with hot water.</i>

68
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:27,582
GANWOLJAE, WHERE THE WIND RESTS

69
00:03:27,665 --> 00:03:29,667
<i>They sell roasted eggs</i>
<i>and instant rice too.</i>

70
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,502
<i>Let's eat at 10:30 a.m.</i>

71
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:32,962
LUNCH SCHEDULED FOR 10:30 A.M.

72
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:35,006
We'll eat <i>ramyeon</i> and eggs there.

73
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:36,799
We'll set off again at 11:00 a.m.

74
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:38,551
We'll check our gear before we leave.

75
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,011
And we should arrive at 12:00 p.m.

76
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:41,221
At 12:00 p.m.

77
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,056
Hey, at the top of Sinbulsan,

78
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:45,308
let's shout "Yahoo!"

79
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:47,477
We haven't done that yet.

80
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,937
They said we can't shout.

81
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:50,355
We can't do that nowadays?

82
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:51,606
HIKING ETIQUETTE

83
00:03:51,689 --> 00:03:54,275
REFRAIN FROM SHOUTING
TO NOT STARTLE WILD ANIMALS OR HIKERS

84
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,526
A silent "Yahoo."

85
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,654
A silent "Yahoo" sounds good.

86
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:00,073
DEPART FROM SINBULSAN
AFTER SILENT YAHOO AT 12:05 P.M.

87
00:04:00,156 --> 00:04:03,201
So if we walk the ridge
to the next peak, that'll take…

88
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,661
About one and a half hours.

89
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,204
The time it takes to see it?

90
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:08,623
We're fast, so let's be there by 1:30 p.m.

91
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,124
We'll cut it by five minutes.

92
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:12,168
It's the last peak and mountain,

93
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:15,088
so tell the viewers
how you felt being on the show.

94
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:18,508
Let's finish all of that in one minute.

95
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:22,011
Of course, we know
the production crew works very hard.

96
00:04:22,095 --> 00:04:24,264
But last time, at Baengnokdam,

97
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:25,682
they wasted a lot of time.

98
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,850
Well, it was exactly nine minutes.

99
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:29,560
-Really?
-Yes.

100
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,229
It must've felt long because we waited.

101
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:32,730
It was nine minutes minus the wait?

102
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,649
When these two arrived,

103
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:36,776
we just took a quick photo
and went straight down.

104
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:38,569
Is that so? Thank you for your hard work.

105
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:39,487
EMBARRASSED GARDEN

106
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:43,408
I look forward to your cooperation
this time around too.

107
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,702
And tomorrow…

108
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:47,287
The most important thing is

109
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,747
we'll be hiking together tomorrow.

110
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:52,917
That means Hyun-yong
is going to explain stuff to us again.

111
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,794
You all are too kindhearted,

112
00:04:54,877 --> 00:04:56,587
but at least for that moment,

113
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:58,548
put that kindness of yours away.

114
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:00,008
DECLARES NO SIGHTSEEING

115
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,801
Why are we going to the mountains then?

116
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,803
PRESIDENT TAR'S SHARP WORDS

117
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:04,929
Aren't we going for that?

118
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,764
That's why it's driving me mad.

119
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:12,812
THE ONE SUPPOSEDLY GOING MAD

120
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:16,149
CAUGHT RED-HANDED
TAKING PHOTOS OF THE MOUNTAIN

121
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,191
What's gotten into you?

122
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:18,484
It's just for the sake of it.

123
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:20,528
It is pretty beautiful here.

124
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:21,446
SHY GARDEN

125
00:05:22,196 --> 00:05:26,367
This place definitely has
the prettiest view.

126
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,202
The reed field is pretty here.

127
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:29,912
I see why they'd shoot TV shows here.

128
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:32,206
Honestly, I kind of like these.

129
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:37,420
This is actually the first time
I've thought a mountain looked nice.

130
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:38,963
This mountain is the best one.

131
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,006
Ulsan is nice.

132
00:05:40,089 --> 00:05:42,508
CAR, THE GARDEN WILL BE DRIVEN MAD
BY YEONGNAM ALPS' BEAUTY

133
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,385
Was it three hours to descend?

134
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:45,762
-Two and a half.
-Two and a half?

135
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:48,890
Let's aim to finish the descent
by 4:00 p.m.

136
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:49,974
We'll pick up the pace.

137
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:52,518
We always finish descending
around 4:00 p.m.

138
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:55,104
DESCEND CLUB HAS DEVELOPED A ROUTINE

139
00:05:55,188 --> 00:05:56,189
Let's go with this.

140
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:03,446
APPROVED BY THE MANAGER

141
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:05,948
The president should sign it too.

142
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:08,284
You need to sign after me to finalize it.

143
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:09,577
In this small spot.

144
00:06:09,660 --> 00:06:11,245
TINY

145
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:13,081
I think you signed in my spot.

146
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:15,792
That's a cool signature.

147
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:16,834
It looks like graffiti.

148
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:17,960
APPROVED BY PRESIDENT TAR

149
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:19,587
Mine's simple.

150
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:22,131
MINISTER OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS APPROVES

151
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,633
It can't be simpler than mine.

152
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:26,552
Hey, what is that?

153
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:27,470
-Dowoon.
-It's "Do."

154
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:29,138
Isn't this just a checkmark?

155
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:30,056
SUPER SIMPLE

156
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:32,016
This is actually a "DW."

157
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,559
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT APPROVES

158
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:35,645
The schedule looks good today.

159
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:38,272
A THOROUGH PLAN BEFITTING
OF THE 3-PEAK CHALLENGE

160
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:43,277
THE YEONGNAM ALPS
CLIMBING SCHEDULE IS COMPLETE

161
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,447
Good night, guys.

162
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:48,574
Good night. Good work today.

163
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:53,871
EVERYONE GOES TO BED

164
00:07:00,753 --> 00:07:04,799
CHAE AND CHAE HAVE BREAKFAST

165
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,261
EATING EGGS AND BANANAS

166
00:07:09,095 --> 00:07:11,889
DOWOON IS STILL ASLEEP

167
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:14,267
GROANING

168
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:17,478
GRUNTS

169
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:22,191
I had a dream
where we climbed Mount Everest.

170
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:26,237
Gosh, how horrible.

171
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:30,616
CAN'T STOP THINKING ABOUT
HIS HIKING NIGHTMARE

172
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:33,661
EVEN THOUGH HE'S STILL HALF-ASLEEP

173
00:07:33,744 --> 00:07:36,539
MAKES SURE TO LAYER
HIS CLOTHES THOROUGHLY

174
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:42,670
CAR, THE GARDEN IS READY

175
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:45,590
You have the legs of a model.

176
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:49,719
You have the upper body of a UFC fighter,
but your lower body is that of a model.

177
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,221
Someone said this to me last time.

178
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:53,848
It was the first time we ever met.

179
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:55,475
They looked at my legs

180
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:58,102
and said, "You have Nine Muses' legs."

181
00:08:02,273 --> 00:08:04,275
"Your upper body is pretty big."

182
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:05,526
THE WORST PHYSIQUE FOR HIKING

183
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:08,070
"But you have Nine Muses' legs."

184
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,656
Hello. The weather is nice.

185
00:08:11,449 --> 00:08:13,451
Why are your pants down so low?

186
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:14,577
Sorry?

187
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,953
The waist is too big.

188
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,163
-Is that the reason?
-Yes.

189
00:08:17,246 --> 00:08:19,749
-Is it unintentional sagging?
-Yes.

190
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:22,210
I don't sag my pants when I hike.
It's too cold.

191
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:26,464
While doing this show, I started spending
less effort on being stylish.

192
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:28,758
That's how hard it is.

193
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:29,967
Hiking, that is.

194
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:34,055
It makes someone who loves to look cool
pull up his pants.

195
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:36,057
That's what hiking does.

196
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:38,851
Gosh.

197
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,687
EXCLAIMING

198
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,105
THE REAL MODEL IS HERE

199
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:44,357
You're K2 personified.

200
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:46,150
Come on, you're the same.

201
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,152
I'm in the minor leagues with K2.

202
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,905
"Minor leagues."

203
00:08:50,988 --> 00:08:52,740
Watch K2 send me an official letter.

204
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:54,742
"We ask that you not wear

205
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:58,496
our brand's products
on a show ever again."

206
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:01,666
I heard you had a good dream, Dowoon.

207
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,376
-Sorry?
-I heard you had a good dream.

208
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:04,585
I woke up screaming.

209
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,755
Since it was in your dream,
I should send you there.

210
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,757
What are you talking about?

211
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:14,178
For the first time,
I got to sleep for seven hours

212
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:16,055
before going hiking.

213
00:09:16,138 --> 00:09:18,516
It's so nice to get some good sleep
before we hike.

214
00:09:19,141 --> 00:09:20,142
I'm feeling great.

215
00:09:20,226 --> 00:09:21,769
Yes, I feel really good.

216
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:25,106
THEY SET OFF IN GOOD CONDITION

217
00:09:25,189 --> 00:09:27,858
Today, we just need to tough it out

218
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:30,486
during school hours.

219
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:31,571
That's right.

220
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:34,615
Goodness.

221
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:36,659
It sure is cool.

222
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:39,704
I don't see any high mountains.

223
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:42,331
Maybe we're climbing three of those.

224
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,416
I think so.

225
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:46,002
-That must be the route.
-Yes.

226
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:47,837
Along the ridge.

227
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:51,382
Still, let's warm up our ankles and knees

228
00:09:51,465 --> 00:09:52,550
so we won't get injured.

229
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:53,759
Let's do it.

230
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:56,512
143 BAENAEMUDEUNGGOL-GIL, SANGBUK-MYEON,
ULJU-GUN, ULSAN, KOREA

231
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:58,139
BAENAEGOGAE PARKING LOT

232
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:01,225
I bet we won't need crampons at all today.

233
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:02,852
No, I don't think we'll need them.

234
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:06,606
I think we'll only have to wear
a thin pair of gloves too.

235
00:10:06,689 --> 00:10:07,940
Yeah, a thin pair.

236
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:09,108
Exactly.

237
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:13,321
TODAY'S HIKE IS DIFFERENT FROM THE OTHERS

238
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:17,491
A NON-FROZEN TRAIL
THAT DOESN'T NEED CRAMPONS

239
00:10:18,075 --> 00:10:21,662
THE SUN WAS ALREADY UP 1 HOUR AGO

240
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:25,791
WARM ENOUGH OF A TEMPERATURE AT 2.1°C
FOR MOUNTAIN BIRDS TO WAKE UP

241
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:30,713
GENTLE WIND BLOWING SOUTHWEST
AT 0.9 M/S

242
00:10:31,964 --> 00:10:33,841
BUT IN REALITY, IT'S A STRONG WIND

243
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:35,301
The wind's stronger than expected.

244
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:37,970
NARROW TERRAIN AND HIGH ALTITUDE
MAKE THE WIND BLOW HARDER

245
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,347
Things aren't right.

246
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:40,723
What is this?

247
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:42,850
We have to go up quickly.

248
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,644
BEFORE GOING UP

249
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,853
PEAK 1

250
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:47,521
GANWOLSAN

251
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:48,439
PEAK 2

252
00:10:48,522 --> 00:10:50,691
SINBULSAN

253
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:51,609
PEAK 3

254
00:10:51,692 --> 00:10:53,778
YEONGCHUKSAN

255
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:56,822
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE
TODAY'S HIKING TRAIL

256
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:59,825
IF YOU CLIMB THE ENDLESS STAIRS

257
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:03,579
AND PASS THROUGH THE SCREE TRAIL

258
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,373
PEAK 1 CONQUERED

259
00:11:05,456 --> 00:11:06,457
GANWOLSAN

260
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:11,712
DESCEND ALONG
GOLDEN SILVER GRASS FIELDS

261
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:15,508
GANWOLJAE, THE SILVER GRASS FIELD
BETWEEN GANWOLSAN AND SINBULSAN'S RIDGES

262
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:17,927
TOWARD PEAK 2

263
00:11:19,011 --> 00:11:21,180
ASCENDING AGAIN

264
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:26,685
KEEP GOING UP AND DOWN ALONG THE RIDGE

265
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:28,479
PEAK 2 CONQUERED

266
00:11:28,562 --> 00:11:29,939
SINBULSAN

267
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:35,152
HIKE ALONG THE RIDGE
BETWEEN THE SILVER GRASS FIELDS AGAIN

268
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:40,032
CLIMB OVER THE FOLLOWING PATH
WITH BIG ROCKS

269
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:41,700
PEAK 3 CONQUERED

270
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,035
YEONGCHUKSAN

271
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:45,788
BAENAEGOGAE PARKING LOT, GANWOLSAN,
SINBULSAN, YEONGCHUKSAN

272
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:48,791
HIKING DISTANCE: ABOUT 10 KM
ESTIMATED TIME: 5 HOURS AND 30 MINUTES

273
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:53,796
HIKING STARTS

274
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,798
It's going to be a bit chilly.

275
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:56,715
Yeah.

276
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:59,009
It's an aggressive wind.

277
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:01,345
It's cold.

278
00:12:01,429 --> 00:12:03,139
A BIT CHILLY DUE TO THE STRONG WIND

279
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:05,599
We're not wearing crampons.

280
00:12:05,683 --> 00:12:07,643
THEIR FIRST HIKE WITHOUT CRAMPONS

281
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:08,853
It's nice.

282
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:12,314
THE SEONGPANAK TEAM
TAKES LEAD SIDE BY SIDE

283
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,442
Hey, slow down!

284
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:16,235
Sorry?

285
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:19,196
Someone said something.

286
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,823
Someone said something?

287
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:22,283
Go slow.

288
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,576
IT'S PRODUCER NAH

289
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,661
PRODUCER NAH'S PLEA WAS BURIED BY THE WIND

290
00:12:25,744 --> 00:12:27,079
Someone said, "Go slow."

291
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,706
It's just some old guy from town.

292
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,710
LONELY

293
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,253
What's with this incline?

294
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:39,300
TODAY'S HIKING TRAIL
IS STEEP FROM THE START

295
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:41,093
It's crazy from the get-go.

296
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:44,805
SIGHING

297
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:47,308
It feels strange without crampons.

298
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:52,938
THEY WALK PAST THE STEEP INCLINE
IN AN ENVIRONMENT DIFFERENT FROM BEFORE

299
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,816
It's all stairs from this point,
and it'll be tough.

300
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,945
FROM HERE TO THE HIGHEST PEAK

301
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:04,617
THEY'LL CLIMB ABOUT 1 KM OF STAIRS

302
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:09,371
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN

303
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:14,043
MIDDLE: DOWOON

304
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:18,923
TAIL: TARZZAN

305
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:23,886
WALKING STRONG IN A 2-1-1 FORMATION

306
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:29,850
This really is like a StairMaster here.

307
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:35,814
TAKING OFF HIS HAT

308
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:38,734
<i>The path had stairs from the start.</i>

309
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,611
It was warm too.

310
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:44,698
And certain parts of your muscles
are used for climbing stairs,

311
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:45,950
like on a StairMaster.

312
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:48,494
So I got hot very suddenly and quickly.

313
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,041
<i>It was better than I thought.</i>

314
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:55,501
The reason was

315
00:13:55,584 --> 00:13:59,296
there had been so many stairs
that were even more terrible.

316
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:02,925
I was just grateful
that there wasn't any snow.

317
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:06,554
We have to go up anyway,
so it's great to do it without snow.

318
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:10,140
It reminded me
of the stairs from hell in Hallasan.

319
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:11,684
I mean the Stairway to Heaven.

320
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:16,063
CRACKS UP

321
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:21,694
<i>When I think about that…</i>

322
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:24,947
Dowoon and I know what we're both thinking
just by looking at each other.

323
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:29,577
DOWOON'S POSTURE
IS THE SAME AS IT WAS THEN

324
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:31,245
Gosh.

325
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:33,455
Gosh!

326
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:36,083
Here it comes.

327
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,713
CAR-THE QUICKLY FEELS SOMETHING

328
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:42,882
SIGHING

329
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:43,924
Gosh.

330
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:50,222
YOU CAN GO AHEAD

331
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,390
Go ahead.

332
00:14:54,018 --> 00:15:00,524
MR. NINE MUSES IS THE FIRST
TO TIRE OUT AGAIN TODAY

333
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:03,068
He must be tired.

334
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,320
THE MEMBERS WAIT FOR HIM

335
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:06,822
This isn't easy.

336
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:10,367
HE CATCHES HIS BREATH AND STARTS WALKING

337
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:12,494
We're going to match your pace,

338
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:13,579
so move to the front.

339
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:14,538
Okay.

340
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:16,707
When I stop, you stop.

341
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:17,791
Got it.

342
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,668
When you stop, we'll rest.

343
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:25,049
THEY SET OFF AGAIN

344
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:29,094
TODAY'S PACEMAKER

345
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,140
<i>The rule of Descend Club</i>

346
00:15:33,223 --> 00:15:36,393
is to match the pace
of the slowest person.

347
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:40,189
It's our unwritten rule.

348
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:42,733
And matching Car-the's pace

349
00:15:42,816 --> 00:15:45,027
actually turned out
to be the right choice.

350
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:49,323
WALKING IN STEP WITH THE PACEMAKER

351
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:52,284
CHAE-MIN

352
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:55,412
THOSE FOLLOWING BEHIND

353
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:58,707
THE CAMERA OPERATORS
AND PRODUCERS WALKING AHEAD

354
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:01,627
THEY ALL MATCH CAR, THE GARDEN'S PACE

355
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:05,881
AND TAKE A SLOW HIKE

356
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:08,968
<i>I got the feeling</i>
<i>that we should match Jung-won's pace</i>

357
00:16:09,051 --> 00:16:11,804
<i>if we wanted to complete</i>
<i>all three peaks together.</i>

358
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:13,263
It was okay, actually.

359
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:14,974
We should work as a team.

360
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,185
Can we have a break
to take some layers off?

361
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:19,103
Sure.

362
00:16:19,728 --> 00:16:21,188
I'm already starting to sweat.

363
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,358
He's lucky. I'm not sweating.

364
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:25,275
Really?

365
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,735
I'm too cold to sweat.

366
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:28,946
Walking slowly is much better.

367
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,197
Right?

368
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,448
This time,

369
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:33,742
I really went at my own pace.

370
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:36,578
I thought,
"It's fine as long as we go up, right?"

371
00:16:37,454 --> 00:16:40,499
"The production crew
didn't tell me to hurry up either."

372
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:43,585
The other guys go up fast
because they're energetic.

373
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:45,504
They even wait for me too.

374
00:16:45,587 --> 00:16:47,256
It's not like anyone is rushing me.

375
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:49,967
But it'll be a nuisance if I go too slow,

376
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:54,096
so I thought I should go
at a reasonable and safe pace.

377
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:56,015
I don't need to walk fast.

378
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,099
I can't.

379
00:16:57,182 --> 00:16:58,308
I can't go.

380
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,019
-I give up.
-You go at your own pace.

381
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:05,566
ANOTHER PERSON
WHO WALKED UP AT HIS OWN PACE

382
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:10,404
Is it doable for you guys?

383
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:11,780
Are you okay?

384
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:14,324
It's better since I'm walking slowly.

385
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:15,826
This is slow?

386
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:19,913
SETTING OFF AGAIN

387
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:23,000
STILL HIKING SLOWLY

388
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:25,377
If you go slow, you're invincible.

389
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:29,757
-What did he say?
-"If you go slow, you're invincible."

390
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,760
If you go slow, you're invincible?

391
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:33,719
That's right.

392
00:17:33,802 --> 00:17:35,888
"IF YOU GO SLOW, YOU'RE INVINCIBLE"
-YOON SEONG-JUNG

393
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:38,849
The stairs here are a bit too much.

394
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:41,101
It's better if you walk slow.

395
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,311
Yes, it's not tiring at all.

396
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:43,228
Yeah.

397
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,897
NOT TIRED THANKS TO THE PACEMAKER

398
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:48,567
Once we get past there,
it'll be the end of the stairs.

399
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:49,985
I don't know if the stairs ending

400
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,153
is a good or bad thing.

401
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:52,613
We'll find out when we get there.

402
00:17:52,696 --> 00:17:54,990
It's called a scree trail,
which has rocks…

403
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,658
Does it make you worn out and screech?

404
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:58,702
SCREE TRAIL

405
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:00,329
SLOPE COMPRISED OF BIG AND SMALL ROCKS

406
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:01,914
FOOTING IS UNSTABLE SO CAUTION NEEDED

407
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:03,415
I told you stairs are better.

408
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:05,667
Stairs are safe at least.

409
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:09,296
Stairs are simple and repetitive.

410
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:12,508
I like simple tasks.

411
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:26,730
THE LONG STRETCH OF STAIRS NEAR AN END

412
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:31,652
Is that the peak? It looks like one.

413
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:37,699
THEY'RE NOT AT THE PEAK YET

414
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:40,702
PEAK 1, GANWOLSAN SUMMIT

415
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,705
CURRENT LOCATION

416
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:46,458
GANWOLSAN, GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA,
SINBULSAN, YEONGCHUKSAN

417
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:47,918
GANWOLSAN 3 KM

418
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:49,378
3 KM LEFT UNTIL PEAK 1

419
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:50,963
This is a scree trail.

420
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:52,381
Watch your ankles.

421
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:54,675
-Okay.
-Be careful when you step on a rock.

422
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:56,426
GOING ONTO THE SCREE TRAIL

423
00:18:57,010 --> 00:19:01,098
A SLOPE COMPOSED OF ROCKS AND DIRT

424
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:09,648
THE SCREE TRAIL CONTINUES ALONG THE RIDGE

425
00:19:10,482 --> 00:19:12,484
The ground feels good here.

426
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,823
The difficulty is rather okay
for a mountain.

427
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:19,324
-Right?
-Yeah.

428
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:22,327
The trail we went on before…

429
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,830
Was it because
we only went on difficult trails?

430
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:27,541
Well, I'm glad there's no snow.

431
00:19:27,624 --> 00:19:28,458
Exactly.

432
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,214
I almost rolled my ankle.

433
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:35,465
What?

434
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:36,633
Did you sprain it?

435
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:39,469
I tweaked it a bit, but it doesn't hurt.

436
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,429
Let's take it slow.

437
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:45,225
IT'S A GENTLE SLOPE, BUT BE CAREFUL
OF ROCKS ON THE SCREE TRAIL

438
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:49,605
SINCE IT'S A RIDGE, IT'S VERY WINDY

439
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:50,689
Goodness.

440
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:55,652
PUTS ON HIS BALACLAVA

441
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:59,072
FIGHTING THE HEADWINDS WITH HIS BARE FACE

442
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:02,576
HE GIVES UP

443
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:08,040
ZIPS UP AND PERFECTLY BLOCKS OUT THE WIND

444
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:14,630
DOWOON, TARZZAN, CHAE-MIN, CAR-THE

445
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:19,760
AS THEY WALK ALONG THE RIDGE

446
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:21,887
Is that the first peak?

447
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:22,846
No.

448
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:24,556
-It is.
-Baenaebong Peak.

449
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:27,643
They don't count this.

450
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:30,604
BAENAEBONG HAS AN ELEVATION BELOW 1,000 M

451
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:32,856
SO IT ISN'T RECOGNIZED
FOR THE COMPLETION CERTIFICATE

452
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:34,775
THEY ARRIVE AT BAENAEBONG

453
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:37,236
This is almost 1,000 m
above sea level already.

454
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:40,072
966 M ABOVE SEA LEVEL

455
00:20:40,864 --> 00:20:43,533
You have 2.6 km left until Ganwolsan.

456
00:20:44,159 --> 00:20:46,578
Where is Ganwolsan?

457
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,664
It's that pointy mountain
you see over there.

458
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,083
They're all pointy though. Hold on.

459
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:52,668
It's the one you see in front of you.

460
00:20:52,751 --> 00:20:53,669
THEY'RE ALL POINTY

461
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:55,003
-The one in the middle?
-Yes.

462
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:58,548
GANWOLSAN SUMMIT
CURRENT LOCATION

463
00:20:58,632 --> 00:20:59,758
-That one?
-Yes.

464
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:02,052
We need to go all the way there
to complete one peak…

465
00:21:02,135 --> 00:21:03,345
That's so damn high.

466
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,056
FULL OF CONCERNS

467
00:21:06,139 --> 00:21:07,933
So on the way down from the first peak,

468
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,351
there's a place to eat, right?

469
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:11,186
-Yes.
-That's pretty far though.

470
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,312
Let's just go.

471
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,605
Come on, let's just go.

472
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,982
Well, let's go.

473
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:18,443
IT WILL TAKE ABOUT 1 HOUR AND 20 MINUTES
TO REACH PEAK 1

474
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:19,528
CURRENT LOCATION

475
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:21,613
THEY'LL GO DOWN FROM BAENAEBONG
AND CLIMB BACK UP

476
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:26,410
DESCENDING FROM BAENAEBONG

477
00:21:26,493 --> 00:21:28,829
I thought we'd come smoothly so far.

478
00:21:28,912 --> 00:21:29,746
-Exactly.
-Exactly.

479
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,626
Watch out for the branches.

480
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:38,005
THE PATH IS SURROUNDED BY SHORT TREES

481
00:21:38,088 --> 00:21:40,465
182 CM TALL

482
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:42,884
190 CM TALL

483
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:45,304
177.8 CM TALL

484
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,723
179 CM TALL

485
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:51,101
THE MEN WITH AN AVERAGE HEIGHT
OF 182.2 CM EVADE THEM WELL

486
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:52,102
Watch your head.

487
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:54,062
This area's a bit…

488
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:56,440
You could scratch your face.

489
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:57,607
Exactly. Be careful.

490
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:00,319
THE TUNNEL OF TREE CONTINUES

491
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:02,571
OUCH

492
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:03,905
What a difficult path.

493
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:06,241
THE TOWERING CHAE-MIN ALMOST GOT SCRATCHED

494
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,242
OUCH

495
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:14,916
TALL PEOPLE AT A DISADVANTAGE
WITH THESE MOUNTAIN FEATURES

496
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,586
This area is a bit adventurous.

497
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,297
Dowoon, your shoelaces are untied.

498
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:22,966
Thank you.

499
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:26,011
TIGHTENING THE LACES OF HIS HIKING SHOES

500
00:22:26,094 --> 00:22:27,387
Let's go.

501
00:22:27,471 --> 00:22:28,805
SNIFFS

502
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:31,725
ACTUALLY, DOWOON'S REAL PROBLEM WAS…

503
00:22:32,642 --> 00:22:38,565
HIS NOSE AND THROAT WERE IN POOR CONDITION
AT THE START OF THE HIKE

504
00:22:40,942 --> 00:22:42,736
<i>Your rhinitis seemed to give you trouble.</i>

505
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:44,780
Right, my nose.

506
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:47,240
-It suddenly broke down.
-When did it become like that?

507
00:22:47,324 --> 00:22:48,241
I don't know.

508
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:50,035
I need to see the footage.

509
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:52,996
My nose suddenly started to get irritated.

510
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,500
Why is it so downhill now?

511
00:22:56,583 --> 00:22:57,584
We're going down a lot.

512
00:22:57,667 --> 00:22:59,086
That means we need to go up a lot.

513
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:02,172
HOLLOW LAUGH

514
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:05,634
NEGATIVE GARDEN: THIS PATH IS SO…

515
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:08,553
POSITIVE GARDEN: IT'S SO DYNAMIC

516
00:23:09,137 --> 00:23:11,223
I'm behind you, so do worry.

517
00:23:15,143 --> 00:23:16,478
Not "don't worry."

518
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:17,979
Do worry.

519
00:23:18,688 --> 00:23:19,940
Still,

520
00:23:20,023 --> 00:23:22,067
Car-the must not be too exhausted.

521
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:23,735
-Me?
-You're talking.

522
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:25,112
Seeing how I'm yapping?

523
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:27,322
I can tell by your mouth.

524
00:23:27,405 --> 00:23:29,157
NATTERING WITH CAR, THE GARDEN
ON EASY HIKES

525
00:23:29,741 --> 00:23:31,243
This is how you can enjoy it a bit.

526
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:33,703
It feels like a hike today.

527
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:35,455
Yeah, it feels good too.

528
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,167
We need to climb that now.

529
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:41,211
Yes, what you see there is Ganwoljae.

530
00:23:41,878 --> 00:23:42,754
We're almost there.

531
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:43,839
We're almost there?

532
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:47,425
ESTIMATED TO TAKE ABOUT 45 MINUTES
TO GET HERE

533
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:48,885
He's a complete liar.

534
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:49,886
A complete lie.

535
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:52,180
We can clearly see it, so what are you…

536
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:54,516
Our producer lies…

537
00:23:54,599 --> 00:23:55,433
A lot.

538
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:59,104
On your left is where we were yesterday
in downtown Ulsan.

539
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:01,022
We were there yesterday?

540
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:02,440
It's where we hung out yesterday.

541
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:03,859
Where did we hang out yesterday?

542
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:05,235
Yeah, where did we hang out?

543
00:24:06,027 --> 00:24:07,696
Where did we hang out yesterday?

544
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:08,655
LAUGHING

545
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:09,698
RUNNING AWAY

546
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:12,117
-We hung out yesterday?
-He's not too sure either.

547
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:13,827
So he just points and walks away.

548
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:16,371
Tarzzan, do you see Ulsan on your left?

549
00:24:17,038 --> 00:24:18,707
-Yes.
-Can you tell what area that is?

550
00:24:19,207 --> 00:24:20,208
Of course not.

551
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:21,126
Really?

552
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:22,460
What area is that?

553
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:24,629
EVEN THE ONE FROM ULSAN DOESN'T KNOW

554
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,506
FACT: CAN'T SEE
WHERE THEY HUNG OUT FROM HERE

555
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:27,841
He's just showed a random area.

556
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:32,512
Because of the reflection of the light…

557
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:34,806
-Reflection of the light?
-What?

558
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:36,641
We can see everything clearly.

559
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:39,728
DOPAMINE BLAST FROM LAUGHING

560
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:42,606
LAME EXCUSE

561
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:45,275
Goodness, it's so windy.

562
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:53,325
ASCENDING AGAIN
THROUGH THE WIND AND TREES

563
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:56,369
This mountain is difficult
in a different way.

564
00:24:57,204 --> 00:24:58,288
Right.

565
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:00,916
The path's rough here.

566
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,585
GOING DOWN ANOTHER ROCK WITH A BIG DROP

567
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:04,669
Which way do you go?

568
00:25:06,755 --> 00:25:08,840
This must be the highlight of the trail.

569
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:13,929
TARZZAN USES THE HIKING POLES

570
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:18,099
DOWOON TAKES BIG STEPS TOO

571
00:25:18,683 --> 00:25:22,562
"MOUNTAINS AND LIFE ALLOW MORE
TO THOSE WHO ARE BRAVE"

572
00:25:22,646 --> 00:25:26,483
MOUNTAINEER UM HONG-GIL

573
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:29,486
Doesn't it feel like a hard section
will be at the end?

574
00:25:30,737 --> 00:25:32,072
-I think so.
-Yeah.

575
00:25:32,906 --> 00:25:33,907
I think there will be.

576
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:42,958
ALMOST AT PEAK 1

577
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:46,628
GRUNTING

578
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:49,172
SIGHING

579
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:50,757
MORE SIGHING

580
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:51,841
What is this place?

581
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:56,012
FROM TARZZAN'S CAM

582
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:58,098
This is basically rock climbing.

583
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:07,649
What's with this place?

584
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,242
SIGHING

585
00:26:21,496 --> 00:26:28,461
PASSING THE TOUGH SECTION AT THE END

586
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:32,340
The first of three peaks.

587
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:33,425
Peak One.

588
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:36,511
Ganwolsan.

589
00:26:36,594 --> 00:26:38,513
THEY ARRIVE AT PEAK 1, GANWOLSAN

590
00:26:38,596 --> 00:26:39,931
-It's beautiful here.
-Yes.

591
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:43,393
GANWOLSAN

592
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:46,604
WITH AN ELEVATION OF 1,069 M,
A FAMOUS YEONGNAM ALPS MOUNTAIN

593
00:26:46,688 --> 00:26:48,523
KNOWN FOR THE SILVER GRASS FIELD
"GANWOLJAE"

594
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:54,612
GANWOLSAN

595
00:26:54,696 --> 00:26:56,448
CURRENT LOCATION
GANWOLSAN

596
00:26:56,531 --> 00:26:57,824
HIKING TO SUMMIT

597
00:26:57,907 --> 00:27:00,368
PEAK 1 GANWOLSAN CONQUERED

598
00:27:03,121 --> 00:27:04,539
-Let's go down now.
-Okay.

599
00:27:04,622 --> 00:27:05,623
Hold on…

600
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:07,375
I explained yesterday…

601
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:09,377
-What is it?
-What did you explain?

602
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:10,462
For every peak…

603
00:27:11,379 --> 00:27:12,589
RUMMAGING

604
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:13,923
It's a cash prize!

605
00:27:14,674 --> 00:27:15,592
It's a cash prize!

606
00:27:16,134 --> 00:27:17,302
Hey, they're giving us money.

607
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:18,219
Gosh!

608
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:19,304
Really?

609
00:27:19,387 --> 00:27:20,430
IN SEOUL BEFORE HIKE

610
00:27:20,513 --> 00:27:21,806
It's a three-peak challenge.

611
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:23,683
For each peak you reach,

612
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,310
we'll give you a cash prize.

613
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:26,686
-You'll give us money?
-What?

614
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:28,480
-Just a little. For team dinners.
-Money?

615
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:32,901
One envelope for each peak.
We wanted to give you a little bit.

616
00:27:34,194 --> 00:27:35,862
Manager Car, thank you for your efforts.

617
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:38,156
HANDS OUT FIRST ENVELOPE
FOR CLIMBING PEAK 1

618
00:27:38,239 --> 00:27:39,491
How much is it?

619
00:27:39,574 --> 00:27:40,784
-What?
-It's 40,000 won.

620
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:42,786
So 10,000 per person.

621
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:44,829
10,000 WON X 4 = 40,000 WON

622
00:27:44,913 --> 00:27:45,747
LOSING ENERGY

623
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,040
Still, for the team dinner…

624
00:27:47,123 --> 00:27:47,957
Yeah, sure.

625
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:49,209
SURPRISED BY THE AMOUNT

626
00:27:49,292 --> 00:27:50,543
You'll get one for each peak.

627
00:27:50,627 --> 00:27:52,212
Can you complain for us, Jung-won?

628
00:27:52,921 --> 00:27:54,130
Look.

629
00:27:54,214 --> 00:27:56,216
How long have we been hiking?
An hour and a half?

630
00:27:56,299 --> 00:27:57,634
A bit longer than two hours.

631
00:27:57,717 --> 00:27:59,177
Then, our hourly wage is 5,000 won.

632
00:27:59,260 --> 00:28:00,678
ROUGHLY 5,000 WON AN HOUR

633
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:02,806
<i>It was worse than not getting paid at all.</i>

634
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:04,808
"Are they making fun of us?"

635
00:28:04,891 --> 00:28:07,685
How can the wage be 5,000 won per hour
in this day and age?

636
00:28:07,769 --> 00:28:10,939
Back when I had my first part-time job,
it was still more than that.

637
00:28:11,981 --> 00:28:14,192
I'm sorry, but the amount wasn't much,

638
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:15,485
so it didn't really register.

639
00:28:16,736 --> 00:28:19,155
DISAPPOINTED SIGH

640
00:28:19,781 --> 00:28:21,324
-Minimum wage is…
-We'll hang onto it.

641
00:28:21,408 --> 00:28:22,534
It's still money though.

642
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:24,869
BOTH PARTIES HAVE A BAD TASTE
IN THEIR MOUTHS

643
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:26,204
SHOWING OFF

644
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:28,081
ANYWAYS, FIRST ENVELOPE RECEIVED

645
00:28:28,164 --> 00:28:31,000
THEY DEPART FROM GANWOLSAN'S SUMMIT

646
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:32,335
Let's go.

647
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:35,588
HEADING TO GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA
ABOUT 20 MINUTES AWAY

648
00:28:35,672 --> 00:28:37,132
Is it downhill all the way there?

649
00:28:37,215 --> 00:28:39,092
Yes, it's almost all downhill.

650
00:28:40,301 --> 00:28:42,137
Watch out for your knees and ankles.

651
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:44,472
THEY'LL CONTINUE ON A GENTLE DOWNHILL

652
00:28:45,181 --> 00:28:52,063
LIKE THE PATH,
THE WIND BECOMES GENTLE TOO

653
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,066
It's warm and then it's cold.

654
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,152
This mountain seems to have mood swings.

655
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,069
Yeah.

656
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:03,950
THE CHANGING WINDS MAKE IT TOUGH

657
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:10,123
BUT THE RISE AND FALL OF THE RIDGE
CREATES BEAUTIFUL SCENERY

658
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:19,299
DOWOON CAPTURES THE VIEW WITH HIS CAMERA

659
00:29:19,382 --> 00:29:20,884
I see stairs over there.

660
00:29:23,219 --> 00:29:26,222
Do you see the brown area down there?

661
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:27,557
Yes.

662
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:29,392
That's the silver grass field.

663
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:31,978
And that's the Ganwoljae Service Area.

664
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:33,062
We'll have lunch there.

665
00:29:33,146 --> 00:29:34,147
Near the parking lot?

666
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:35,148
That's right.

667
00:29:35,231 --> 00:29:36,816
It looks very well-maintained.

668
00:29:36,900 --> 00:29:37,734
Yes.

669
00:29:37,817 --> 00:29:39,235
GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA

670
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:41,946
This is the biggest silver grass field
in Korea.

671
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:45,825
<i>Crash Landing on You</i> was here?

672
00:29:45,909 --> 00:29:48,161
This is where they filmed
the paragliding scene.

673
00:29:48,244 --> 00:29:49,537
I remember. In Episode One.

674
00:29:49,621 --> 00:29:50,455
Yes.

675
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:52,791
Does she paraglide
and end up in North Korea?

676
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:54,709
This is where they filmed that scene.

677
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,586
SON YE-JIN PARAGLIDED HERE IN THE SHOW

678
00:29:56,669 --> 00:29:58,213
How did they get up here?

679
00:29:59,130 --> 00:30:00,381
A parking lot's over there.

680
00:30:01,257 --> 00:30:05,261
CARS HALFWAY UP A MOUNTAIN

681
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:06,888
What on earth?

682
00:30:08,014 --> 00:30:10,016
THE PARKING LOT IS USED BY PARK STAFF

683
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:12,310
ONLY VEHICLES WITH PRIOR AUTHORIZATION
ARE ALLOWED

684
00:30:12,393 --> 00:30:13,603
IT MAKES HIM LOSE ENERGY

685
00:30:13,686 --> 00:30:14,896
There's a parking lot.

686
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:16,272
Shall we go?

687
00:30:16,356 --> 00:30:21,653
DESCEND CLUB WALKS
TO THE SILVER GRASS FIELD

688
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:29,244
GANWOLJAE

689
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:31,162
AT AN ELEVATION OF 900 M

690
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:33,957
THE PASS CONNECTS GANWOLSAN AND SINBULSAN

691
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:39,879
MANY HIKERS VISIT TO SEE
THE VAST SILVER GRASS FIELD

692
00:31:00,149 --> 00:31:05,488
A VIEW OF DOWNTOWN ULSAN AND THE OCEAN

693
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:11,870
<i>The golden silver grass field</i>
<i>stretched out like this.</i>

694
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:14,581
<i>It was so beautiful and enchanting.</i>

695
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:24,382
<i>I thought, "I didn't know</i>
<i>there was a place like this in Korea."</i>

696
00:31:26,009 --> 00:31:28,887
I thought it'd be really nice
to capture it on camera.

697
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:31,097
Later, whether for a TV show or a movie,

698
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:34,267
I thought it'd be really beautiful
to shoot in a place like this.

699
00:31:39,397 --> 00:31:40,273
<i>It was beautiful.</i>

700
00:31:40,356 --> 00:31:41,941
You come with your family,

701
00:31:42,025 --> 00:31:45,278
and you happily talk
with each other like this while hiking.

702
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:47,030
As you eat your packed lunches,

703
00:31:47,113 --> 00:31:48,865
you'd go, "The view is amazing, isn't it?"

704
00:31:48,948 --> 00:31:50,783
That would be perfect.

705
00:31:50,867 --> 00:31:54,370
DO YOU REMEMBER COMING HERE
WHEN YOU WERE YOUNG?

706
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:56,289
<i>I think I vaguely remember it.</i>

707
00:31:56,372 --> 00:31:58,958
I do remember whining.

708
00:31:59,042 --> 00:32:00,877
"How much further do we have to go?"

709
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,503
<i>I remember saying that.</i>

710
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:11,471
LITTLE LEE CHAE-WON
CLIMBED THE YEONGNAM ALPS

711
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:13,389
I don't know if it was the same field,

712
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:14,641
but I do remember that.

713
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:17,685
It's so beautiful here.

714
00:32:18,311 --> 00:32:19,687
Isn't it beautiful?

715
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:20,605
Yes.

716
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:23,608
What?

717
00:32:24,233 --> 00:32:25,151
"Isn't it beautiful?"

718
00:32:25,234 --> 00:32:26,069
"Yes."

719
00:32:26,152 --> 00:32:28,237
He answered his own question.

720
00:32:32,408 --> 00:32:35,119
What do you think? Doesn't it look
like the Alps of Yeongnam?

721
00:32:36,871 --> 00:32:37,872
I don't know.

722
00:32:42,335 --> 00:32:44,212
I don't know what the Alps look like.

723
00:32:44,295 --> 00:32:48,049
How would I know
if this is the Alps of Yeongnam?

724
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:50,760
But it's definitely different
from the snowy mountains, right?

725
00:32:50,843 --> 00:32:52,136
Yes. It is pretty here.

726
00:32:54,097 --> 00:32:56,015
I feel better here
than I did on snowy trails.

727
00:32:56,516 --> 00:33:00,687
It definitely is the prettiest here.

728
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:01,604
I agree.

729
00:33:02,230 --> 00:33:03,815
It makes you feel a bit calm.

730
00:33:03,898 --> 00:33:07,819
Being too high up honestly scares me.

731
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:10,488
The silver grass field is beautiful.

732
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:12,240
I can see why they shot a TV show here.

733
00:33:12,323 --> 00:33:13,241
Exactly.

734
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:14,409
It's cool!

735
00:33:17,495 --> 00:33:18,663
It's cool.

736
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:22,291
Great job, everyone.

737
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:23,459
That's one peak.

738
00:33:23,543 --> 00:33:27,714
THEY ARRIVE AT GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA

739
00:33:32,176 --> 00:33:33,219
Peak One, out.

740
00:33:33,803 --> 00:33:35,179
"Peak One, out."

741
00:33:35,763 --> 00:33:38,016
THEY'LL HAVE LUNCH HERE

742
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:41,060
A PLEASANT INDOOR AREA

743
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:45,523
IT BECOMES A SHELTER FOR HIKERS

744
00:33:47,567 --> 00:33:49,152
They sell snacks and eggs here.

745
00:33:49,235 --> 00:33:50,695
-I want eggs.
-Me too.

746
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,448
THE SHOP HAS FOOD
FOR SIMPLE MEALS AND SNACKS

747
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:54,824
CUP NOODLES
2,000 WON

748
00:33:54,907 --> 00:33:56,284
INSTANT RICE

749
00:33:57,702 --> 00:33:59,162
CHOCOLATE BARS
1,000 WON

750
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:01,622
THEY SELL SIMPLE HIKING ACCESSORIES TOO

751
00:34:02,248 --> 00:34:04,709
I'll get one Shin Ramyun and an egg.

752
00:34:05,418 --> 00:34:08,046
If anyone needs more water,
we can each get another bottle.

753
00:34:08,129 --> 00:34:10,631
THEY EACH TAKE A CUP OF INSTANT NOODLES

754
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:11,883
Should we use our cash prize?

755
00:34:12,508 --> 00:34:13,509
-Let's do it.
-Okay.

756
00:34:13,593 --> 00:34:14,427
THEY AGREE

757
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:19,807
PAYS 15,000 WON WITH THEIR CASH PRIZE

758
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:20,808
The cash prize!

759
00:34:20,892 --> 00:34:22,769
You're using it right away?

760
00:34:23,936 --> 00:34:25,313
Yes, since it offends me.

761
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:31,152
PURCHASED 4 CUP NOODLES,
4 ROASTED EGGS, AND 1 BOTTLE OF WATER

762
