"The crater is so deep. Take a photo."
That's the vibe.

900
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:23,522
"You're not taking a photo?
It's Baengnokdam!"

901
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:25,524
That's what it feels like.

902
00:41:26,692 --> 00:41:27,693
But this one?

903
00:41:29,987 --> 00:41:31,989
"Hello."

904
00:41:32,072 --> 00:41:33,199
"It's very relaxing."

905
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:34,200
"It's not that high."

906
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:37,077
THE YEONGNAM ALPS' VIEW MADE
EVEN CAR, THE GARDEN'S HEART MELT

907
00:41:38,787 --> 00:41:39,788
Yahoo.

908
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:43,459
Yahoo.

909
00:41:43,959 --> 00:41:46,212
WITH CHEERFUL ENERGY

910
00:41:46,295 --> 00:41:49,924
THEY START WALKING TOWARD SINBULSAN AGAIN

911
00:41:51,509 --> 00:41:53,719
-Hello.
-Hello.

912
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:55,304
Good luck.

913
00:41:55,387 --> 00:41:58,015
GOOD MANNERS LEARNED FROM HALLASAN

914
00:42:00,059 --> 00:42:04,230
ALONG THE RIDGE WHERE THE WIND HAS SETTLED

915
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:06,899
<i>On the ridge to the second peak,</i>

916
00:42:06,982 --> 00:42:11,445
the ridge path
was mostly like flat ground.

917
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:14,490
I didn't even run out of breath
in that area.

918
00:42:15,115 --> 00:42:15,950
It's over there.

919
00:42:17,660 --> 00:42:18,577
Looks like it.

920
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:21,705
THEY'RE AT EYE-LEVEL
WITH THE SUMMIT OF SINBULSAN

921
00:42:22,706 --> 00:42:25,167
THE DESIRE TO TAKE IN WITH THEIR EYES

922
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:29,255
THE SCENERY THEY SEE AS THEY WALK ALONG

923
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:31,507
This is the best mountain.

924
00:42:32,466 --> 00:42:34,051
The path is paved well.

925
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:36,095
WOODEN STAIRS WITH RUBBER MATS
TO PREVENT SLIPPING

926
00:42:36,178 --> 00:42:37,888
Yeah, this will help you not slip.

927
00:42:38,472 --> 00:42:40,808
Every part of this trail
was made thoughtfully.

928
00:42:40,891 --> 00:42:42,893
YOU SEEMED TO REALLY LIKE
THE YEONGNAM ALPS

929
00:42:43,811 --> 00:42:45,938
The facilities were made
very thoughtfully.

930
00:42:46,689 --> 00:42:47,898
Starting with the restrooms.

931
00:42:47,982 --> 00:42:51,110
They even had rubber mats in place
on the trail at times.

932
00:42:51,694 --> 00:42:53,153
The Yeongnam Alps were outstanding.

933
00:42:54,822 --> 00:42:57,908
Chae-min, what did I say mountains
overlapping like that were called?

934
00:42:57,992 --> 00:42:58,826
Sorry?

935
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,911
It's when you see
layers and layers of mountains.

936
00:43:01,745 --> 00:43:02,871
You said that before?

937
00:43:03,831 --> 00:43:05,082
Pork belly layer mountains.

938
00:43:06,125 --> 00:43:07,042
Does anyone remember?

939
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:08,043
You said that?

940
00:43:08,127 --> 00:43:09,920
You didn't. You just made it up.

941
00:43:10,004 --> 00:43:11,463
I explained it twice on Taebaeksan.

942
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:12,548
THE ANSWER IS

943
00:43:13,048 --> 00:43:14,592
<i>Sangeurime.</i>

944
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:15,926
We've never heard of it before.

945
00:43:16,010 --> 00:43:17,177
THEY JUST WANT TO KEEP GOING

946
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:19,930
-You never told us.
-We've never heard of it before.

947
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:23,601
The mountains you see beyond mountains
are called <i>sangeurime.</i>

948
00:43:23,684 --> 00:43:24,518
"San?"

949
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:26,437
<i>Sangeurime.</i> It's a pure Korean word.

950
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:28,564
EVERYONE HAS FORGOTTEN
THE MEMORY OF TAEBAEKSAN

951
00:43:28,647 --> 00:43:30,107
SANGEURIME OR MOUNTAIN SILHOUETTE

952
00:43:30,190 --> 00:43:33,277
THE FAINT VIEW OF DISTANT MOUNTAINS
LINED UP IN LAYERS LIKE SHADOWS

953
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:35,904
THEY DON'T RECALL AND WALK
WITH SANGEURIME IN THE BACKGROUND

954
00:43:36,655 --> 00:43:37,990
CLOSE TO THE SUMMIT OF SINBULSAN

955
00:43:38,073 --> 00:43:39,116
We're almost there.

956
00:43:39,742 --> 00:43:41,076
We're at the second peak now?

957
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:43,495
I guess they'll give us money again.

958
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:44,413
Right, the money.

959
00:43:44,496 --> 00:43:46,624
THE SECOND CASH PRIZE
IS WAITING AT THE PEAK

960
00:43:47,833 --> 00:43:49,460
Shall we run to the destination?

961
00:43:50,461 --> 00:43:51,295
Go ahead.

962
00:43:55,049 --> 00:43:57,217
HE SUDDENLY STARTS RUNNING ON THE TRAIL

963
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:00,888
Models are on another level.

964
