rather than someone like me.

1004
00:45:25,013 --> 00:45:26,098
She said, "He's handsome!"

1005
00:45:26,181 --> 00:45:27,516
So I said, "Aren't I handsome?"

1006
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:28,434
And she said, "No!"

1007
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:29,935
"What?"

1008
00:45:30,561 --> 00:45:31,687
HURT

1009
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:32,604
"No"?

1010
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:35,274
She had clear standards.

1011
00:45:35,357 --> 00:45:37,693
Ulsan has clear standards.

1012
00:45:37,776 --> 00:45:39,486
Actually, I rather liked that.

1013
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,905
It's better than those
forcing themselves to say it.

1014
00:45:43,031 --> 00:45:44,116
Honestly, I know it too.

1015
00:45:44,825 --> 00:45:46,118
If they say I'm very handsome,

1016
00:45:46,952 --> 00:45:48,036
I go, "You're lying."

1017
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:51,457
Congratulations.

1018
00:45:51,957 --> 00:45:53,000
Good job, everyone.

1019
00:45:53,083 --> 00:45:54,543
That's two out of three peaks!

1020
00:45:54,626 --> 00:46:01,341
THEY ARRIVE AT PEAK 2, SINBULSAN

1021
00:46:01,425 --> 00:46:02,259
SINBULSAN

1022
00:46:02,342 --> 00:46:03,886
ELEVATION OF 1,159 M
TALLEST OF 3 PEAKS

1023
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:05,137
IN TOP 100 MOUNTAINS OF KOREA

1024
00:46:05,220 --> 00:46:06,763
ALSO ITS SILVER GRASS FIELD

1025
00:46:06,847 --> 00:46:09,016
IS IN THE TWELVE SCENIC PLACES OF ULSAN

1026
00:46:12,853 --> 00:46:13,770
SINBULSAN

1027
00:46:13,854 --> 00:46:15,314
HIKING TO SUMMIT

1028
00:46:15,397 --> 00:46:17,983
PEAK 2 SINBULSAN CONQUERED

1029
00:46:18,066 --> 00:46:19,985
HANDS OUT SECOND ENVELOPE
FOR CLIMBING PEAK 2

1030
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:20,903
Open it.

1031
00:46:20,986 --> 00:46:22,821
You have to give us
20,000 won each this time.

1032
00:46:22,905 --> 00:46:24,865
WISHING FOR DOUBLE THE AMOUNT FOR PEAK 2

1033
00:46:24,948 --> 00:46:29,578
HOW MUCH IS THE SECOND CASH PRIZE?

1034
00:46:29,661 --> 00:46:30,537
Peak Two.

1035
00:46:32,789 --> 00:46:35,292
SECOND CASH PRIZE
40,000 WON

1036
00:46:35,375 --> 00:46:37,794
THEIR REACTIONS ARE AS FROZEN
AS THEIR WAGES

1037
00:46:38,378 --> 00:46:40,714
TRUDGING

1038
00:46:41,298 --> 00:46:43,342
EXCITED WITHOUT KNOWING WHAT'S GOING ON

1039
00:46:43,425 --> 00:46:45,302
They're cheering you on back there.

1040
00:46:45,385 --> 00:46:49,431
A WAVE OF SUPPORT FOR THE FROZEN WAGES?

1041
00:46:49,515 --> 00:46:51,016
Lastly, the third peak.

1042
00:46:51,099 --> 00:46:53,101
-Where is it?
-Look over there.

1043
00:46:53,185 --> 00:46:56,396
In the middle to the left,
one looks a bit like a cliff.

1044
00:46:56,480 --> 00:47:00,150
That's on Yeongchuksan,
our third and final peak.

1045
00:47:00,734 --> 00:47:02,444
-That cliff?
-Yes.

1046
00:47:02,528 --> 00:47:03,779
Once you get to Yeongchuksan,

1047
00:47:03,862 --> 00:47:06,698
you will have conquered
three peaks of the Yeongnam Alps.

1048
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:09,952
CURRENT LOCATION

1049
00:47:10,035 --> 00:47:11,912
TO THE FINAL DESTINATION, YEONGCHUKSAN

1050
00:47:11,995 --> 00:47:14,331
IT STARTS WITH A DESCENT

1051
00:47:14,957 --> 00:47:16,750
BELOW IS THE SILVER GRASS PLATEAU,
SINBULJAE

1052
00:47:22,005 --> 00:47:23,507
ONCE THEY PASS SINBULJAE

1053
00:47:24,591 --> 00:47:26,301
THEY'LL ENCOUNTER A LONG STRETCH OF RIDGE

1054
00:47:28,804 --> 00:47:31,098
AFTER CLIMBING UP AND DOWN THE RIDGE

1055
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:33,559
A ROUGH ROCKY PATH SIGNALS END

1056
00:47:37,187 --> 00:47:38,355
YOU CAN'T LET YOUR GUARD DOWN

1057
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:44,319
THE TRAIL TO END
TODAY'S CONSECUTIVE HIKES ON A HIGH NOTE

1058
00:47:44,903 --> 00:47:47,698
THEY DEPART FROM SINBULSAN'S SUMMIT

1059
00:47:48,282 --> 00:47:49,241
You're so handsome.

1060
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:50,826
Thank you.

1061
00:47:50,909 --> 00:47:53,078
THE FIRST TO ANSWER GETS THE COMPLIMENT

1062
00:47:53,870 --> 00:47:54,746
You're so handsome.

1063
00:47:54,830 --> 00:47:55,664
Thank you.

1064
00:47:55,747 --> 00:47:58,083
THE ACTUAL COMPLIMENT TARGET
ISN'T BOTHERED BY THE STEAL

1065
00:47:58,875 --> 00:48:00,836
I'm so glad the weather is nice.

1066
00:48:00,919 --> 00:48:03,880
RESUMING HIKING HAPPILY

1067
00:48:03,964 --> 00:48:05,716
I'm really happy.

1068
00:48:05,799 --> 00:48:08,135
LEAD: THE SEONGPANAK TEAM PAIR AGAIN

1069
00:48:08,218 --> 00:48:10,637
TAIL: THE GWANEUMSA TEAM PAIR AGAIN

1070
00:48:10,721 --> 00:48:12,889
THEY HEAD TOWARD SINBULJAE
WITH THEIR HALLASAN PARTNERS

1071
00:48:12,973 --> 00:48:15,017
IT STARTS WITH A ROCKY PATH
ON A GENTLE SLOPE

1072
00:48:17,269 --> 00:48:19,187
ALONG THE WOODEN STAIRS

1073
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:21,315
GOING DOWN FOR 20 MINUTES STRAIGHT

1074
00:48:22,691 --> 00:48:23,775
It's nice here.

1075
00:48:25,193 --> 00:48:27,154
The trail is easy now.

1076
00:48:27,237 --> 00:48:28,238
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

1077
00:48:28,322 --> 00:48:31,241
ENJOYING THE VIEW WHILE WALKING

1078
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:34,661
SEARCHING

1079
00:48:36,496 --> 00:48:38,665
YOON DORAEMON TAKES OUT
SOMETHING FROM HIS POCKET

1080
00:48:39,499 --> 00:48:42,878
HE TRIES HARD TO PEEL IT AS HE WALKS DOWN

1081
00:48:44,713 --> 00:48:47,299
HIS FAVORITE TRAIL FOOD,
SWEET RED BEAN JELLY

1082
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:51,470
PRECIOUS TO HIM

1083
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:57,517
A BITE OF SWEET RED BEAN JELLY
TO REFUEL ENERGY

1084
00:48:58,727 --> 00:49:01,605
ANOTHER BITE

1085
00:49:02,689 --> 00:49:05,108
THIRD BITE

1086
00:49:05,817 --> 00:49:09,488
REFUELING FINISHED IN THREE BITES

1087
00:49:13,950 --> 00:49:17,913
HE PUTS THE TRASH BACK IN HIS POCKET

1088
00:49:18,497 --> 00:49:21,667
HE WALKS ON AFTER RECHARGING

1089
00:49:21,750 --> 00:49:23,293
It's a dog!

1090
00:49:24,586 --> 00:49:27,130
HE SPOTS A DOG HIKING

1091
00:49:27,214 --> 00:49:29,966
HARD FOR A DOG LOVER TO JUST PASS BY

1092
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:34,388
AS STILL AS A STONE WHILE WATCHING THE DOG

1093
00:49:42,062 --> 00:49:44,523
AFTER BEING COMFORTED
BY THE DOG, HE RETURNS

1094
00:49:52,531 --> 00:49:55,117
HIS RHINITIS IS STILL THERE

1095
00:49:56,368 --> 00:49:59,037
I haven't been sweating much
because the wind keeps blowing.

1096
00:49:59,121 --> 00:50:00,122
Right.

1097
00:50:01,164 --> 00:50:02,541
As I sweat, it just cools.

1098
00:50:03,917 --> 00:50:08,213
AFTER WALKING ALONG WITH THE COOL BREEZE

1099
00:50:16,388 --> 00:50:19,641
THEY EVENTUALLY ARRIVE AT THIS PLACE

1100
00:50:21,893 --> 00:50:24,229
A PATH WHERE THE WIND PASSES THROUGH

1101
00:50:25,772 --> 00:50:28,775
THE SILVER GRASS PLATEAU
WHERE FOUR ROADS MEET

1102
00:50:41,788 --> 00:50:46,126
THEY ARRIVE AT SINBULJAE

1103
00:50:46,209 --> 00:50:48,253
SNIFFLING

1104
00:50:48,336 --> 00:50:49,379
-Dowoon.
-Yes?

1105
00:50:49,463 --> 00:50:51,214
-Are you okay?
-I think I have a head cold.

1106
00:50:51,298 --> 00:50:52,466
Did you catch a cold?

1107
00:50:52,549 --> 00:50:54,926
Maybe? My nose is so itchy.

1108
00:50:55,594 --> 00:50:56,970
Do you have allergies?

1109
00:50:57,053 --> 00:50:58,221
No, not that I know of.

1110
00:50:58,305 --> 00:51:00,015
I think you have allergies, Dowoon.

1111
00:51:00,098 --> 00:51:01,057
Really?

1112
00:51:01,558 --> 00:51:03,268
You're allergic to mountains.

1113
00:51:03,351 --> 00:51:05,353
DIAGNOSIS COMPLETE

1114
00:51:06,104 --> 00:51:09,900
Anyway, we can make it
to the third and final peak in an hour.

1115
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:13,028
Okay, let's speed up for the homestretch.

1116
00:51:14,529 --> 00:51:17,949
AWAKENED BY THE NEWS
THAT THERE'S ONLY 1 HOUR LEFT TO GO

1117
00:51:18,784 --> 00:51:20,494
Okay, everyone. Make sure to follow along.

1118
00:51:21,077 --> 00:51:22,245
Let's move out.

1119
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:23,163
ENERGY IS GOOD

1120
00:51:23,246 --> 00:51:25,081
Let's see how tough
the Gwaneumsa trail was.

1121
00:51:25,165 --> 00:51:26,541
Okay, I'll go really fast.

1122
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:28,335
SEONGPANAK TEAM'S PROVOCATION
FIRES HIM UP

1123
00:51:28,418 --> 00:51:30,545
I need to run to get it out of my system.

1124
00:51:30,629 --> 00:51:31,463
Here we go.

1125
00:51:31,546 --> 00:51:32,964
LEAVING SINBULJAE AFTER A REST

1126
00:51:35,133 --> 00:51:37,344
LEAD: AN AWAKENED DOWOON

1127
00:51:37,427 --> 00:51:40,847
MIDDLE: TARZZAN ALSO PICKS UP THE PACE

1128
00:51:40,931 --> 00:51:44,351
TAIL: CAR, THE GARDEN AND CHAE-MIN

1129
00:51:44,434 --> 00:51:48,188
MINISTER OF TRANSPORT'S NOSE
HAS SLIGHTLY CLEARED

1130
00:51:49,064 --> 00:51:50,857
You're getting in my way.

1131
00:51:51,983 --> 00:51:55,111
OVERCOMES HIS MOUNTAIN ALLERGY
AND GOES FULL THROTTLE ON THE STAIRS

1132
00:51:56,571 --> 00:51:59,491
CURRENT LOCATION

1133
00:51:59,574 --> 00:52:01,993
Let me know anytime you need trail food.

1134
00:52:02,077 --> 00:52:05,580
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT IS IN CHARGE
OF THEIR TRAIL FOOD AGAIN TODAY

1135
00:52:05,664 --> 00:52:07,123
I want spaghetti.

1136
00:52:07,207 --> 00:52:08,708
I don't have that.

1137
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:11,545
GOING DOWNHILL AGAIN

1138
00:52:28,311 --> 00:52:29,479
It's 1.4 km?

1139
00:52:29,563 --> 00:52:31,606
Yes, the summit of Yeongchuksan
is 1.4 km away.

1140
00:52:31,690 --> 00:52:35,360
TOWARD THE FINAL AND THIRD PEAK

1141
00:52:35,443 --> 00:52:39,155
THEY CLIMB THE RIDGE HIGH IN THE CLOUDS

1142
00:52:39,656 --> 00:52:41,658
FAR OFF IN THE DISTANCE

1143
00:52:41,741 --> 00:52:43,618
LOOKING AT THE SUMMIT AS THEY GO

1144
00:52:44,202 --> 00:52:45,871
Gosh, this is practically a cliff.

1145
00:52:45,954 --> 00:52:47,789
DOCENT: DO YOU SEE THAT OVER THERE?

1146
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:49,749
You can see
the starting point of the mountain.

1147
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:50,834
Sorry?

1148
00:52:51,918 --> 00:52:52,752
Isn't it cool?

1149
00:52:52,836 --> 00:52:54,004
What is?

1150
00:52:55,380 --> 00:52:56,256
We came from there…

1151
00:52:56,756 --> 00:52:58,592
What? Don't leave.

1152
00:52:58,675 --> 00:52:59,968
ESCAPES

1153
00:53:00,051 --> 00:53:01,052
Wait for us.

1154
00:53:01,136 --> 00:53:01,970
Wait for us!

1155
00:53:02,637 --> 00:53:03,471
I'll go first.

1156
00:53:03,555 --> 00:53:05,223
EX-DOCENT: I WON'T EXPLAIN ANYMORE

1157
00:53:05,307 --> 00:53:06,600
We were going at a good pace.

1158
00:53:06,683 --> 00:53:07,517
Exactly.

1159
00:53:08,602 --> 00:53:09,603
You know what I think?

1160
00:53:10,228 --> 00:53:12,439
I think I'm allergic to his talks.

1161
00:53:13,481 --> 00:53:14,608
My nose keeps running.

1162
00:53:14,691 --> 00:53:15,692
That's exactly it.

1163
00:53:16,401 --> 00:53:17,235
That's it.

1164
00:53:20,322 --> 00:53:21,406
This is crazy.

1165
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:25,744
BEHIND THE YOUNGER MEMBERS IN THE LEAD

1166
00:53:26,578 --> 00:53:29,623
AND ALBEIT A BIT SLOW,
HE SEEMED TO KEEP UP WELL

1167
00:53:29,706 --> 00:53:33,001
LEAD: TARZZAN

1168
00:53:33,084 --> 00:53:36,379
MIDDLE 1: DOWOON

1169
00:53:36,463 --> 00:53:39,758
MIDDLE 2: CHAE-MIN

1170
00:53:41,509 --> 00:53:44,054
ALL THE WAY AT THE TAIL: CAR, THE GARDEN

1171
00:53:44,137 --> 00:53:45,221
Car-the.

1172
00:53:47,015 --> 00:53:49,309
THEY FINALLY SPOT HIM NOW

1173
00:53:49,392 --> 00:53:51,436
Man, I'm in such a bad mood.

1174
00:53:52,687 --> 00:53:54,689
THE PACEMAKER CAN ONLY FOLLOW THEIR PACE

1175
00:53:54,773 --> 00:53:55,732
Let's go.

1176
00:53:55,815 --> 00:53:57,859
We should let Car-the go first.

1177
00:53:57,943 --> 00:53:59,194
All right.

1178
00:53:59,277 --> 00:54:00,320
Let's match his pace.

1179
00:54:00,403 --> 00:54:01,529
Take it slow.

1180
00:54:02,197 --> 00:54:06,034
THE PACEMAKER FINALLY RETURNS TO HIS PLACE

1181
00:54:06,534 --> 00:54:08,453
There's a lesson to learn from hiking.

1182
00:54:08,536 --> 00:54:10,330
-What?
-Hiking teaches a lesson.

1183
00:54:10,413 --> 00:54:12,165
HE HAD TIME TO CONTEMPLATE WHILE FOLLOWING

1184
00:54:12,874 --> 00:54:14,209
You have to go at your own pace.

1185
00:54:14,292 --> 00:54:16,670
"GO AT YOUR OWN PACE"
SINGER CAR, THE GARDEN

1186
00:54:16,753 --> 00:54:19,089
APPLYING THE LESSON LEARNED TODAY

1187
00:54:19,798 --> 00:54:20,757
So maybe, you know,

1188
00:54:21,383 --> 00:54:22,968
Producer Nah is doing it right.

1189
00:54:26,388 --> 00:54:27,472
<i>Walking slowly…</i>

1190
00:54:27,555 --> 00:54:28,890
Then, I want to rest.

1191
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:30,850
<i>And falling behind.</i>

1192
00:54:30,934 --> 00:54:32,435
That actually was the answer.

1193
00:54:33,269 --> 00:54:34,980
NOT SURE IF THAT'S A COMPLIMENT OR NOT

1194
00:54:35,063 --> 00:54:36,398
He's doing it right.

1195
00:54:37,065 --> 00:54:38,733
By the way, where's Producer Nah?

1196
00:54:38,817 --> 00:54:40,402
I think he's way behind us.

1197
00:54:40,902 --> 00:54:43,530
No, I think he took a car down
from that rest stop earlier.

1198
00:54:44,364 --> 00:54:48,326
WITH QUESTIONS OF PRODUCER NAH'S
UNKNOWN WHEREABOUTS

1199
00:54:50,370 --> 00:54:52,122
We have the final 300 m left.

1200
00:54:52,205 --> 00:54:53,832
EXCITED HOOTS

1201
00:54:53,915 --> 00:54:54,749
YEONGCHUKSAN 0.3 KM

1202
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:56,418
THEY HAPPILY PASS THE 0.3 KM SIGN

1203
00:54:58,336 --> 00:54:59,963
AS SOON AS THEY PASS BY,

1204
00:55:01,548 --> 00:55:04,968
AN UPHILL SCREE TRAIL APPEARS
FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WHILE

1205
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:09,180
TO INDICATE THE START OF THIS ROAD

1206
00:55:10,890 --> 00:55:13,143
A RIDGE WITH A GENTLE SLOPE

1207
00:55:14,227 --> 00:55:17,355
A SMOOTH SILVER GRASS ROAD

1208
00:55:18,440 --> 00:55:21,192
NONE OF THOSE ARE PRESENT HERE

1209
00:55:25,071 --> 00:55:30,869
THE START OF THE CRUX
RIGHT BEFORE THE THIRD PEAK

1210
00:55:32,662 --> 00:55:35,331
THE FINAL SPURT TO PEAK 3

1211
00:55:35,415 --> 00:55:39,127
5 HOURS AND 21 MINUTES HAVE PASSED

1212
00:55:42,922 --> 00:55:46,051
<i>I was running out of stamina</i>
<i>during the last climb.</i>

1213
00:55:46,134 --> 00:55:48,470
I felt the adversity.

1214
00:55:48,553 --> 00:55:50,472
It was all rocks.

1215
00:55:50,555 --> 00:55:53,224
ROCKS

1216
00:55:54,893 --> 00:55:56,269
EXHALING

1217
00:55:57,854 --> 00:55:59,981
AFTER ONLY WALKING
ON DIRT AND WOODEN STAIRS FOR A BIT

1218
00:56:00,648 --> 00:56:02,233
EXHALING

1219
00:56:02,317 --> 00:56:05,070
ESPECIALLY WHEN THEIR FEET TOUCH
THE GROUND, THEY FEEL MORE FATIGUED

1220
00:56:06,654 --> 00:56:08,448
IT ISN'T EASY TO SPEED UP

1221
00:56:09,908 --> 00:56:11,785
SHAKING HIS HEAD

1222
00:56:12,869 --> 00:56:15,080
THE SUMMIT SEEMS SO CLOSE YET IT'S SO FAR

1223
00:56:17,582 --> 00:56:18,458
Goodness.

1224
00:56:22,962 --> 00:56:24,506
SIGHING

1225
00:56:25,924 --> 00:56:28,343
ON THE VERGE OF RUNNING OUT OF STAMINA

1226
00:56:29,094 --> 00:56:31,805
THEY ARRIVE
JUST A FEW STEPS AWAY FROM THE PEAK

1227
00:56:31,888 --> 00:56:32,889
What is this?

1228
00:56:35,558 --> 00:56:36,935
It's a cliff.

1229
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:39,062
We'll need to use our hands…

1230
00:56:39,145 --> 00:56:41,481
THE SLOPE IS PRETTY MUCH
LIKE THAT OF ROCK CLIMBING

1231
00:56:45,443 --> 00:56:48,404
ONCE THEY CLIMB THE FINAL CLIFF

1232
00:56:52,617 --> 00:56:54,828
-It's on your right.
-We've arrived at Yeongchuksan!

1233
00:56:54,911 --> 00:56:58,039
THEY ARRIVE AT PEAK 3, YEONGCHUKSAN

1234
00:56:58,123 --> 00:56:59,332
Good job, everyone.

1235
00:56:59,415 --> 00:57:00,333
Well done!

1236
00:57:00,416 --> 00:57:01,918
-Well done, everyone.
-Great job.

1237
00:57:02,502 --> 00:57:03,545
We're in Yangsan now.

1238
00:57:06,464 --> 00:57:08,133
YEONGCHUKSAN

1239
00:57:14,180 --> 00:57:16,432
YEONGCHUKSAN
CONNECTS TO GANWOLSAN AND SINBULSAN

1240
00:57:16,516 --> 00:57:18,351
THE FINAL PEAK OF THE CHALLENGE

1241
00:57:18,434 --> 00:57:19,686
TONGDOSA TEMPLE IS LOCATED HERE

1242
00:57:19,769 --> 00:57:22,689
The Yeongnam Alps' three-peak challenge.

1243
00:57:22,772 --> 00:57:24,065
You did it!

1244
00:57:24,149 --> 00:57:26,776
THE YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE
COMPLETE

1245
00:57:29,195 --> 00:57:30,029
Let's sit down.

1246
00:57:31,614 --> 00:57:34,242
PLOPPING DOWN AS SOON AS THEY ARRIVE

1247
00:57:34,325 --> 00:57:36,578
You secured a great spot.

1248
00:57:36,661 --> 00:57:37,495
Just nice.

1249
00:57:37,579 --> 00:57:39,539
GOT HIS STONE BED

1250
00:57:39,622 --> 00:57:40,665
THIRD CASH PRIZE

1251
00:57:40,748 --> 00:57:41,749
-Manager Car.
-I'm beat.

1252
00:57:41,833 --> 00:57:42,667
Thank you.

1253
00:57:42,750 --> 00:57:44,836
HANDS OUT THIRD ENVELOPE
FOR CLIMBING PEAK 3

1254
00:57:44,919 --> 00:57:46,796
Will the final one have more money?

1255
00:57:47,338 --> 00:57:48,715
-A bonus?
-Right.

1256
00:57:48,798 --> 00:57:49,674
What?

1257
00:57:49,757 --> 00:57:50,592
There's more!

1258
00:57:50,675 --> 00:57:52,677
HOPEFUL

1259
00:57:53,261 --> 00:57:54,637
-It's 80,000 won.
-So, 20,000 each.

1260
00:57:54,721 --> 00:57:55,847
Nice.

1261
00:57:55,930 --> 00:57:57,056
-Thank you.
-No problem.

1262
00:57:57,140 --> 00:57:58,224
Thank you.

1263
00:57:59,350 --> 00:58:00,393
-President Tar.
-Yes?

1264
00:58:00,477 --> 00:58:03,229
When we planned the hike yesterday,

1265
00:58:03,313 --> 00:58:07,400
you promised to talk about
how you felt about hiking for one minute.

1266
00:58:07,484 --> 00:58:08,651
-Right.
-What?

1267
00:58:09,194 --> 00:58:10,737
You planned that last night.

1268
00:58:10,820 --> 00:58:13,865
Wasn't that saying goodbye to the viewers
since it's the last mountain?

1269
00:58:13,948 --> 00:58:15,241
FINAL APPROVER SUDDENLY CHANGES

1270
00:58:15,325 --> 00:58:16,534
Yeah, the final episode.

1271
00:58:18,870 --> 00:58:20,997
The Yeongnam Alps
were designed very thoughtfully.

1272
00:58:21,498 --> 00:58:23,041
They have good stairs.

1273
00:58:24,000 --> 00:58:26,711
It's a mountain that's easy to hike.

1274
00:58:27,378 --> 00:58:28,671
Ulsan is good.

1275
00:58:30,006 --> 00:58:31,549
-Ulsan is good.
-Right?

1276
00:58:31,633 --> 00:58:33,551
REMARKS THAT MAKE
THE ULSAN NATIVE PROUD

1277
00:58:34,219 --> 00:58:37,805
CAN'T FORGET THE SUMMIT PHOTO

1278
00:58:37,889 --> 00:58:38,890
YEONGCHUKSAN

1279
00:58:38,973 --> 00:58:40,808
Here we go. Let's smile a bit.

1280
00:58:40,892 --> 00:58:41,726
One, two, three.

1281
00:58:41,809 --> 00:58:45,688
THE OLDER MEMBERS ARE OBEDIENT

1282
00:58:45,772 --> 00:58:46,773
Why? Why do you hike?

1283
00:58:46,856 --> 00:58:48,358
THE YOUNGER MEMBERS POSE ON THEIR OWN

1284
00:58:52,904 --> 00:58:54,197
I think I look pretty sexy.

1285
00:58:55,823 --> 00:58:57,158
Pretend you're looking far away.

1286
00:58:57,242 --> 00:58:58,535
SUGGESTING A NEW POSE

1287
00:58:58,618 --> 00:59:01,955
THEY UNDERSTAND RIGHT AWAY NOW

1288
00:59:02,038 --> 00:59:05,416
A PHOTO TAKEN
WHILE LOOKING AT THE FOOTHILLS

1289
00:59:06,543 --> 00:59:07,377
Let's go!

1290
00:59:09,337 --> 00:59:12,340
FINISHING WITH THEIR SIGNATURE POSE

1291
00:59:12,423 --> 00:59:17,262
FEBRUARY 12, 2026, THE YEONGNAM ALPS'
3-PEAK CHALLENGE IS COMPLETE

1292
00:59:17,345 --> 00:59:18,888
YEONGCHUKSAN

1293
00:59:18,972 --> 00:59:19,973
HIKING TO SUMMIT

1294
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:23,184
PEAK 3, YEONGCHUKSAN CONQUERED

1295
00:59:25,144 --> 00:59:27,522
THE YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE
COMPLETE

1296
00:59:27,605 --> 00:59:29,691
THEY START TO DESCEND

1297
00:59:29,774 --> 00:59:31,192
We'll walk down slowly.

1298
00:59:31,276 --> 00:59:32,110
Let's go.

1299
00:59:32,193 --> 00:59:35,280
TODAY'S DESCENDING TRAIL

1300
00:59:35,363 --> 00:59:37,490
YEONGCHUKSAN

1301
00:59:39,033 --> 00:59:40,076
Let's go to Jinae Village.

1302
00:59:40,159 --> 00:59:41,536
DESCEND TO JINAE VILLAGE
ABOUT 6 KM

1303
00:59:41,619 --> 00:59:42,453
YEONGCHUKSAN

1304
00:59:42,537 --> 00:59:45,039
ALONG THE STEEP RIDGE

1305
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:48,418
THE SCREE TRAIL CONTINUES IN THIS SECTION

1306
00:59:48,501 --> 00:59:51,087
THE STAFF'S PICK
THE FINAL CRUX

1307
00:59:53,464 --> 00:59:55,258
GROANING

1308
00:59:56,801 --> 00:59:57,635
This isn't easy.

1309
00:59:57,719 --> 00:59:58,845
ROUGH FROM THE START

1310
00:59:59,971 --> 01:00:01,180
It's very steep.

1311
01:00:02,473 --> 01:00:06,019
FROM CHAE-MIN'S CAM

1312
01:00:07,770 --> 01:00:08,605
Watch out.

1313
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:12,108
Damn.

1314
01:00:12,191 --> 01:00:13,693
Why is it so slippery here?

1315
01:00:14,485 --> 01:00:16,613
The path is not good here.

1316
01:00:16,696 --> 01:00:20,533
ASCENDING IS TOUGH,
AND DESCENDING IS DANGEROUS

1317
01:00:21,951 --> 01:00:22,785
Jung-won.

1318
01:00:22,869 --> 01:00:24,912
No, I'm just testing it.

1319
01:00:24,996 --> 01:00:25,830
Testing the ground.

1320
01:00:25,913 --> 01:00:27,332
HE THOROUGHLY TESTS IT FIRST

1321
01:00:28,374 --> 01:00:31,294
A HIKING CLUB
THAT SPECIALIZES IN DESCENDING

1322
01:00:32,295 --> 01:00:35,214
DESCEND CLUB

1323
01:00:35,298 --> 01:00:36,507
HISTORY OF DESCENTS

1324
01:00:36,591 --> 01:00:37,675
HUIUNGAK SHELTER, SEORAKSAN

1325
01:00:37,759 --> 01:00:38,718
JANGGUNBONG, TAEBAEKSAN

1326
01:00:38,801 --> 01:00:39,677
BAENGNOKDAM, HALLASAN

1327
01:00:39,761 --> 01:00:43,181
THEY DESCENDED TOP-TIER MOUNTAINS

1328
01:00:43,264 --> 01:00:46,225
Things can't be worse than Seoraksan.

1329
01:00:46,309 --> 01:00:47,685
And we hiked that one.

1330
01:00:48,603 --> 01:00:51,439
USING ALL THE DESCENT TIPS AND TRICKS
THEY'VE LEARNED SO FAR

1331
01:00:51,522 --> 01:00:55,401
TIP 1: USE LONG POLES

1332
01:00:57,153 --> 01:00:59,572
TIP 2: TAKE SHORT STRIDES

1333
01:01:00,948 --> 01:01:03,534
TIP 3: BEND YOUR KNEES
AND LOWER YOUR CENTER OF GRAVITY

1334
01:01:05,370 --> 01:01:07,872
TIP 4: REPLENISH YOUR ENERGY OFTEN
WITH TRAIL FOOD

1335
01:01:08,790 --> 01:01:11,501
DESCENDING STEEP SLOPES
IS A PIECE OF CAKE NOW

1336
01:01:12,085 --> 01:01:13,836
HUMMING

1337
01:01:14,504 --> 01:01:16,506
TIP 5: KEEP YOUR MIND AT EASE

1338
01:01:17,173 --> 01:01:19,759
WERE YOU FEELING HAPPY ON YOUR WAY DOWN?

1339
01:01:19,842 --> 01:01:21,511
Honestly, the Yeongnam Alps were fine.

1340
01:01:21,594 --> 01:01:22,929
I wasn't going to admit it.

1341
01:01:23,012 --> 01:01:25,098
Honestly, they're good mountains.

1342
01:01:25,682 --> 01:01:28,184
GOOD MOUNTAIN GARDEN'S POSTURE
HAS RELAXED TOO

1343
01:01:28,267 --> 01:01:30,687
Car-the seemed to have some stamina left.

1344
01:01:31,187 --> 01:01:33,898
I thought it was
the perfect trail for him.

1345
01:01:34,565 --> 01:01:35,817
YEONGCHUKSAN
CURRENT LOCATION

1346
01:01:35,900 --> 01:01:37,985
THE ROUGH TERRAIN ENDS

1347
01:01:38,069 --> 01:01:40,738
It's nice here.
I hope all the paths are like this.

1348
01:01:40,822 --> 01:01:42,073
Me too.

1349
01:01:42,156 --> 01:01:43,700
NOW THEY DESCEND
THE GENTLE FOREST PATH

1350
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:45,410
It'd be nice if this path continues.

1351
01:01:45,493 --> 01:01:46,327
It's beautiful.

1352
01:01:46,411 --> 01:01:47,412
I hope it continues.

1353
01:01:49,038 --> 01:01:51,416
-This really feels like a hiking trail.
-A walking trail.

1354
01:01:51,499 --> 01:01:53,042
THE FIRST PLEASANT DESCENT IN A WHILE

1355
01:01:54,210 --> 01:01:55,503
I can't believe he ran away.

1356
01:01:57,213 --> 01:01:58,131
He's unbelievable.

1357
01:01:58,214 --> 01:01:59,382
SOMEONE IS NOWHERE TO BE SEEN

1358
01:01:59,465 --> 01:02:00,383
-Jung-won.
-Yeah?

1359
01:02:00,466 --> 01:02:02,343
You know Yung-suk ran off, right?

1360
01:02:02,427 --> 01:02:04,387
Yeah. When did he leave?

1361
01:02:04,470 --> 01:02:07,265
At the peak, we kept waiting…

1362
01:02:07,348 --> 01:02:08,599
We rested for a long time too.

1363
01:02:08,683 --> 01:02:10,059
NOW CERTAIN HE RAN AWAY

1364
01:02:10,143 --> 01:02:11,269
But he still didn't come.

1365
01:02:11,811 --> 01:02:13,438
So, I'm pretty sure he went down

1366
01:02:13,521 --> 01:02:15,231
from where we had lunch.

1367
01:02:15,857 --> 01:02:18,192
I heard something was wrong
with the probiotics he took.

1368
01:02:19,402 --> 01:02:21,529
He can't still be in the toilet, can he?

1369
01:02:22,113 --> 01:02:24,323
It'd be funny if he was.

1370
01:02:26,117 --> 01:02:28,661
ABOUT 3 HOURS AGO
GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA

1371
01:02:28,745 --> 01:02:31,414
I think it's time for me to quit now.

1372
01:02:31,497 --> 01:02:34,083
There might be issues with poop.

1373
01:02:34,167 --> 01:02:36,919
I was in danger twice.

1374
01:02:37,879 --> 01:02:41,174
PRODUCER NAH DESCENDS
FROM GANWOLJAE SERVICE AREA

1375
01:02:42,592 --> 01:02:44,510
I feel so angry all of a sudden.

1376
01:02:44,594 --> 01:02:45,845
-He's a <i>nongtti.</i>
<i>-Nongtti.</i>

1377
01:02:45,928 --> 01:02:46,763
He's a <i>nongtti.</i>

1378
01:02:47,388 --> 01:02:49,348
NONGTTI MEANS SHIRKER
IN GYEONGSANG DIALECT

1379
01:02:49,432 --> 01:02:51,893
I mean, after he took
our badges like that yesterday…

1380
01:02:51,976 --> 01:02:52,810
Exactly.

1381
01:02:52,894 --> 01:02:54,395
VERY REPREHENSIBLE

1382
01:02:54,479 --> 01:02:56,481
I've never seen him
say anything like that before.

1383
01:02:57,273 --> 01:02:59,358
HOW DID YOU FEEL
WHEN PRODUCER NAH DISAPPEARED?

1384
01:03:00,193 --> 01:03:01,861
Of course, I felt very exhausted.

1385
01:03:01,944 --> 01:03:03,905
Whenever I look back,

1386
01:03:03,988 --> 01:03:06,949
he always makes me think,
"I'm doing all right."

1387
01:03:07,533 --> 01:03:10,536
But when he wasn't there…

1388
01:03:11,704 --> 01:03:14,081
Actually, I looked behind very often.

1389
01:03:14,165 --> 01:03:16,667
I always checked if he was coming or not.

1390
01:03:17,168 --> 01:03:19,420
At some point,
we didn't see him climbing up.

1391
01:03:19,504 --> 01:03:20,963
So…

1392
01:03:21,547 --> 01:03:22,757
I realized he abandoned us.

1393
01:03:22,840 --> 01:03:25,718
THE ABANDONED MEMBERS

1394
01:03:26,886 --> 01:03:28,805
GROANING

1395
01:03:29,639 --> 01:03:30,973
Your car could drive up here.

1396
01:03:31,057 --> 01:03:32,350
It easily could.

1397
01:03:32,433 --> 01:03:33,726
Just say the word.

1398
01:03:33,810 --> 01:03:36,062
It'd be cool to rev up here.

1399
01:03:36,145 --> 01:03:36,979
Exactly.

1400
01:03:37,063 --> 01:03:39,774
I probably shouldn't rev up
and run now, right?

1401
01:03:40,733 --> 01:03:42,318
As long as your legs are fine, try it.

1402
01:03:42,944 --> 01:03:44,737
-Should I?
-We can't catch you.

1403
01:03:45,321 --> 01:03:47,532
HE CLEARS HIS NOSE A BIT

1404
01:03:47,615 --> 01:03:48,449
-Careful.
-Careful.

1405
01:03:51,536 --> 01:03:54,288
SPRINTING AT TOP SPEED

1406
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:57,667
FROM DOWOON'S CAM

1407
01:03:57,750 --> 01:04:00,211
SPEED BEFITTING OF HIS TITLE,
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT

1408
01:04:00,294 --> 01:04:03,089
THE FASTEST DESCENT

1409
01:04:03,172 --> 01:04:04,924
Why did he suddenly go crazy like that?

1410
01:04:06,592 --> 01:04:09,262
HE ARRIVES AT THE TRAIL EXIT

1411
01:04:09,762 --> 01:04:10,972
Thank you for running with me.

1412
01:04:11,055 --> 01:04:12,306
EX-SPECIAL FORCES CAMERAMAN

1413
01:04:12,390 --> 01:04:13,224
Damn.

1414
01:04:13,808 --> 01:04:15,268
It's better to come down quickly.

1415
01:04:15,351 --> 01:04:16,435
Exactly.

1416
01:04:17,812 --> 01:04:19,146
I'll save you guys.

1417
01:04:20,523 --> 01:04:21,858
THESE THREE ARE STILL DESCENDING

1418
01:04:21,941 --> 01:04:23,943
There's always an end. I feel that.

1419
01:04:24,819 --> 01:04:26,195
Eventually, it will end.

1420
01:04:27,572 --> 01:04:30,867
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT
IS ON HIS WAY TO FINISH THEIR DESCENT

1421
01:04:32,243 --> 01:04:33,786
They're going to be so happy.

1422
01:04:33,870 --> 01:04:35,288
They're going to be so happy!

1423
01:04:35,371 --> 01:04:37,582
HE LOOKS THE HAPPIEST

1424
01:04:37,665 --> 01:04:38,749
We're almost there now.

1425
01:04:38,833 --> 01:04:40,293
Past the alley here…

1426
01:04:40,376 --> 01:04:41,586
Nice.

1427
01:04:41,669 --> 01:04:42,545
DESCENT ALMOST DONE

1428
01:04:42,628 --> 01:04:44,255
-It's over.
-We just need to go straight.

1429
01:04:45,381 --> 01:04:47,925
A CAR ENTERS THE TRAIL EXIT

1430
01:04:48,009 --> 01:04:49,427
-Gosh.
-Isn't that Dowoon?

1431
01:04:49,510 --> 01:04:51,220
He's here. He came to pick us up.

1432
01:04:51,304 --> 01:04:52,555
I'm here!

1433
01:04:53,055 --> 01:04:55,558
CHEERING

1434
01:04:56,100 --> 01:04:57,518
You did it, Dowoon!

1435
01:04:58,102 --> 01:04:59,061
You did it.

1436
01:04:59,645 --> 01:05:00,980
I don't abandon people!

1437
01:05:01,647 --> 01:05:03,274
FOR THE CAR'S ENTRY INTO THE FOREST ROAD

1438
01:05:03,357 --> 01:05:05,776
PERMISSION WAS RECEIVED IN ADVANCE
FROM YANGSAN CITY HALL

1439
01:05:05,860 --> 01:05:08,529
AFTER 2 HOURS,
ALL MEMBERS COMPLETE DESCENT

1440
01:05:08,613 --> 01:05:09,655
How was it?

1441
01:05:09,739 --> 01:05:10,865
THOUGHTS ON TODAY'S HIKE?

1442
01:05:10,948 --> 01:05:12,867
Honestly, this time,

1443
01:05:13,618 --> 01:05:15,119
the show chose a good location.

1444
01:05:15,202 --> 01:05:17,204
For the first time, I'm grateful

1445
01:05:17,705 --> 01:05:18,956
to the production crew.

1446
01:05:19,457 --> 01:05:21,292
If you put in a little bit of effort,

1447
01:05:22,084 --> 01:05:24,545
there's so much you can see.

1448
01:05:25,129 --> 01:05:28,049
If I find a partner someday,

1449
01:05:28,132 --> 01:05:30,176
I want to climb here with them
and show it off.

1450
01:05:30,760 --> 01:05:32,261
"Have you seen <i>Crash Landing on You?"</i>

1451
01:05:34,513 --> 01:05:38,017
Well, I talked with Car-the,
and he really liked it.

1452
01:05:38,100 --> 01:05:39,936
He liked the mountains in my hometown,

1453
01:05:40,019 --> 01:05:43,606
and that made me feel happy too.

1454
01:05:44,273 --> 01:05:45,107
Yes.

1455
01:05:45,191 --> 01:05:47,985
Do you now have an idea
of why people hike?

1456
01:05:48,861 --> 01:05:51,781
You gave us a badge
after hiking Seoraksan.

1457
01:05:51,864 --> 01:05:53,366
We kept getting them,

1458
01:05:53,449 --> 01:05:55,326
and every time I'd put
a new one on my bag,

1459
01:05:55,993 --> 01:05:57,703
I felt proud of myself.

1460
01:05:57,787 --> 01:05:59,956
Once the bag eventually fills up,

1461
01:06:00,039 --> 01:06:02,208
it'll feel like I've become
a professional mountaineer.

1462
01:06:02,291 --> 01:06:05,503
I felt that psychological sense of reward.

1463
01:06:06,003 --> 01:06:07,630
TAKE A HIKE!

1464
01:06:08,381 --> 01:06:10,967
THEY GRADUALLY COLLECTED
THE REASONS TO HIKE

1465
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:14,095
When you hike,

1466
01:06:16,097 --> 01:06:18,224
it's definitely nice
to show off to your friends.

1467
01:06:18,891 --> 01:06:21,060
When you walk up stairs

1468
01:06:21,143 --> 01:06:23,104
and your friend's suffering,
you can tell them,

1469
01:06:23,187 --> 01:06:25,606
"Come on, man. This is nothing."

1470
01:06:25,690 --> 01:06:27,525
"I've climbed whole mountains."

1471
01:06:27,608 --> 01:06:30,277
It's good for nagging.

1472
01:06:30,861 --> 01:06:33,948
I have something to brag about now.

1473
01:06:34,949 --> 01:06:36,659
My answer will be the same until the end.

1474
01:06:36,742 --> 01:06:38,327
I still don't know why people hike.

1475
01:06:39,453 --> 01:06:41,664
At least Car-the has changed.

1476
01:06:41,747 --> 01:06:43,374
I think it's a big change.

1477
01:06:43,457 --> 01:06:46,585
Do you have an idea now
of why people hike?

1478
01:06:49,839 --> 01:06:50,673
No.

1479
01:06:52,591 --> 01:06:55,594
Honestly, the emotions I felt
on the Yeongnam Alps yesterday?

1480
01:06:57,471 --> 01:06:59,598
I can feel that at Mangwon Hangang Park.

1481
01:07:00,766 --> 01:07:02,393
WHY ON EARTH DO PEOPLE HIKE?
I DON'T KNOW

1482
01:07:02,476 --> 01:07:03,477
I'm serious.

1483
01:07:03,561 --> 01:07:06,480
Yes, you can definitely feel
the same feelings there too.

1484
01:07:07,231 --> 01:07:10,109
I still don't know if climbing's worth it.
I have no idea.

1485
01:07:10,651 --> 01:07:13,112
STILL DOESN'T KNOW WHY PEOPLE HIKE

1486
01:07:15,239 --> 01:07:17,241
SEORAKSAN, TAEBAEKSAN, HALLASAN

1487
01:07:17,324 --> 01:07:19,452
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE

1488
01:07:23,205 --> 01:07:24,040
Good job, everyone.

1489
01:07:24,123 --> 01:07:25,958
Well done, guys. Seriously.

1490
01:07:26,625 --> 01:07:28,502
VERY EXHAUSTED

1491
01:07:28,586 --> 01:07:29,962
Let's go eat some meat.

1492
01:07:30,588 --> 01:07:33,340
HEADING TO DINNER

1493
01:07:33,424 --> 01:07:34,592
JINMI BULGOGI

1494
01:07:34,675 --> 01:07:37,636
DESCEND CLUB'S DESTINATION

1495
01:07:38,763 --> 01:07:41,640
AN EONYANG BULGOGI RESTAURANT
THAT LURES YOU IN WITH ITS SMELL

1496
01:07:42,725 --> 01:07:45,603
WELL-HEATED CHARCOAL FIRE

1497
01:07:46,270 --> 01:07:48,939
GRILLED FLAT-PRESSED BEEF

1498
01:07:55,488 --> 01:07:57,615
EONYANG BULGOGI,
THE SIGNATURE DISH OF EONYANG, ULSAN

1499
01:08:05,915 --> 01:08:09,794
THE SIDES ADD TO THE SAVORY FLAVORS

1500
01:08:11,545 --> 01:08:13,839
A GENEROUSLY PREPARED FULL SPREAD

1501
01:08:18,469 --> 01:08:21,222
DESCEND CLUB ARRIVES

1502
01:08:21,305 --> 01:08:22,890
-Thank you.
-We're here.

1503
01:08:22,973 --> 01:08:24,016
Let's eat.

1504
01:08:24,100 --> 01:08:25,518
-Let's eat.
-I'm so hungry.

1505
01:08:25,601 --> 01:08:27,353
GETTING OUT QUICKLY

1506
01:08:28,104 --> 01:08:30,397
WORN OUT

1507
01:08:31,107 --> 01:08:31,941
What?

1508
01:08:32,817 --> 01:08:34,693
-Producer Nah! What happened?
-Producer Nah.

1509
01:08:34,777 --> 01:08:37,363
-We caught him in the act.
-What did I do wrong? What is it?

1510
01:08:37,446 --> 01:08:39,448
Chae-min, why are you so angry?

1511
01:08:39,532 --> 01:08:40,866
Why are you so mad?

1512
01:08:40,950 --> 01:08:42,076
Where were you earlier?

1513
01:08:43,119 --> 01:08:44,453
Hey, I thought we were friends.

1514
01:08:45,079 --> 01:08:46,330
ANOTHER ANGRY PERSON

1515
01:08:46,413 --> 01:08:47,706
You got changed too.

1516
01:08:48,290 --> 01:08:50,751
We heard some stuff about probiotics.

1517
01:08:50,835 --> 01:08:51,669
Probiotics?

1518
01:08:52,211 --> 01:08:53,254
Let's go inside first.

1519
01:08:53,337 --> 01:08:55,548
The tough thing was…
Gosh, your face is so sunburned.

1520
01:08:55,631 --> 01:08:56,715
What?

1521
01:08:56,799 --> 01:08:57,633
Today…

1522
01:08:58,134 --> 01:08:59,969
It was so tough today.

1523
01:09:00,052 --> 01:09:01,470
Look at how burned he is!

1524
01:09:01,554 --> 01:09:02,429
WHINING

1525
01:09:03,013 --> 01:09:05,558
LET'S EAT FIRST

1526
01:09:06,350 --> 01:09:08,144
-I'm hungry.
-This way, please.

1527
01:09:08,769 --> 01:09:10,271
We'll enjoy the food a bit first.

1528
01:09:27,037 --> 01:09:28,122
It's delicious.

1529
01:09:32,960 --> 01:09:35,212
RICE PAIRED WITH BULGOGI

1530
01:09:35,296 --> 01:09:37,756
This tastes better
if you don't cook it to a crisp.

1531
01:09:37,840 --> 01:09:38,674
Really?

1532
01:09:41,051 --> 01:09:43,721
The bulgogi is held together.

1533
01:09:43,804 --> 01:09:46,307
Ordinary beef bulgogi
has onions and so on.

1534
01:09:46,390 --> 01:09:47,600
THE ULSAN DOCENT

1535
01:09:55,983 --> 01:09:56,984
It's so good.

1536
01:09:57,067 --> 01:09:57,943
This is yours, right?

1537
01:09:58,027 --> 01:09:59,028
It's mine.

1538
01:10:00,070 --> 01:10:04,658
CHOPSTICKS MOVE INVOLUNTARILY
LIKE BREATHING

1539
01:10:04,742 --> 01:10:05,993
You finished one order already?

1540
01:10:06,076 --> 01:10:07,244
THE GRILL IS EMPTY NOW

1541
01:10:07,328 --> 01:10:08,412
Just a moment.

1542
01:10:08,495 --> 01:10:09,997
Thank you. It's delicious, sir.

1543
01:10:10,080 --> 01:10:11,040
Please enjoy your food.

1544
01:10:11,123 --> 01:10:11,999
REFILLED

1545
01:10:12,082 --> 01:10:13,626
This place was on <i>Food Travel</i> too.

1546
01:10:17,588 --> 01:10:18,839
A PIECE OF MEAT

1547
01:10:18,923 --> 01:10:20,633
A BITE OF RICE

1548
01:10:20,716 --> 01:10:22,384
QUICKLY FINISHES A BOWL OF RICE

1549
01:10:23,844 --> 01:10:26,138
THE BULGOGI DISAPPEARS
AS FAST AS THEY DESCENT

1550
01:10:27,056 --> 01:10:29,683
TWO ORDERS FINISHED

1551
01:10:30,434 --> 01:10:31,894
Could you order one more for us?

1552
01:10:32,811 --> 01:10:33,646
Thank you.

1553
01:10:33,729 --> 01:10:34,563
REFILLED AGAIN

1554
01:10:34,647 --> 01:10:36,523
Hyun-yong's the only one
who takes care of us.

1555
01:10:37,691 --> 01:10:41,862
Each meal I've had after descending
with Producer Nah has tasted amazing.

1556
01:10:41,946 --> 01:10:43,155
But today,

1557
01:10:43,239 --> 01:10:45,115
it doesn't taste as good.

1558
01:10:45,741 --> 01:10:47,952
THIRD ORDER OF MEAT
SECOND BOWL OF RICE

1559
01:10:48,035 --> 01:10:51,163
Whatever the reason was,
it's a bit disappointing.

1560
01:10:51,247 --> 01:10:53,832
Because if he had at least told us…

1561
01:10:53,916 --> 01:10:54,875
We were so worried.

1562
01:10:54,959 --> 01:10:56,919
We were always in the same boat,
so it was okay.

1563
01:10:57,002 --> 01:10:58,629
LAUGHING

1564
01:10:58,712 --> 01:11:02,007
Since when did you guys
care so much about me?

1565
01:11:02,091 --> 01:11:03,801
When we were on the last summit,

1566
01:11:03,884 --> 01:11:05,052
we waited for 20 minutes.

1567
01:11:05,135 --> 01:11:06,178
Yeah, and I relied on you.

1568
01:11:06,262 --> 01:11:07,471
"When will Producer Nah come?"

1569
01:11:08,138 --> 01:11:10,516
You guys don't stay on summits for long.

1570
01:11:10,599 --> 01:11:12,434
But we stayed there for a while today.

1571
01:11:13,227 --> 01:11:14,228
We even took pictures.

1572
01:11:17,356 --> 01:11:18,565
IS PRODUCER NAH COMING?

1573
01:11:21,568 --> 01:11:23,946
WHERE DID PRODUCER NAH GO?

1574
01:11:24,029 --> 01:11:26,156
I think of you like my father.

1575
01:11:26,699 --> 01:11:27,700
Dad.

1576
01:11:29,034 --> 01:11:31,620
-Dad, what happened?
-Son.

1577
01:11:31,704 --> 01:11:34,164
First off, you guys went through a lot.

1578
01:11:34,248 --> 01:11:35,624
And so did I.

1579
01:11:35,708 --> 01:11:38,210
We all went through a lot,
so let's give ourselves a hand.

1580
01:11:38,294 --> 01:11:39,128
ALREADY SULKING

1581
01:11:40,129 --> 01:11:41,839
WHATEVER

1582
01:11:41,922 --> 01:11:44,883
FAILED TO LIFT THE MOOD

1583
01:11:44,967 --> 01:11:46,802
What kind of grown-up
has diarrhea like a kid?

1584
01:11:48,429 --> 01:11:51,890
If I were the leader,
I would've at least worn diapers.

1585
01:11:53,517 --> 01:11:56,854
How can you wear diapers on the trail?
I would've worn them if they sold any.

1586
01:11:56,937 --> 01:11:57,938
Had you told us earlier,

1587
01:11:58,022 --> 01:11:59,606
we would've bought them beforehand.

1588
01:11:59,690 --> 01:12:00,691
Exactly.

1589
01:12:00,774 --> 01:12:02,401
THEY DON'T BUY HIS EXCUSE

1590
01:12:03,193 --> 01:12:05,154
THE PRODUCER AND DOCENT
PASSES THE BEEF TARTARE

1591
01:12:05,237 --> 01:12:06,613
Thank you, sir!

1592
01:12:07,406 --> 01:12:08,365
Thank you, Hyun-yong.

1593
01:12:08,991 --> 01:12:10,326
Thank you for the beef tartare.

1594
01:12:10,409 --> 01:12:11,327
BLATANT WARM RESPONSE

1595
01:12:11,410 --> 01:12:13,329
Hyun-yong really is a decent guy.

1596
01:12:13,412 --> 01:12:14,455
He's the real deal.

1597
01:12:14,538 --> 01:12:16,540
He has a big heart, and he's cool.

1598
01:12:16,623 --> 01:12:17,875
We share each other's pain.

1599
01:12:17,958 --> 01:12:20,377
And he must've had it the hardest.

1600
01:12:20,461 --> 01:12:22,504
He's always in the lead

1601
01:12:22,588 --> 01:12:24,298
because he has to stand behind the camera.

1602
01:12:24,381 --> 01:12:25,632
I'm tearing up.

1603
01:12:25,716 --> 01:12:26,967
I'm about to cry.

1604
01:12:27,760 --> 01:12:29,219
-Are you okay?
-Geez.

1605
01:12:31,221 --> 01:12:33,557
Let's do an acrostic poem
with "Park Hyun-yong" later.

1606
01:12:33,640 --> 01:12:35,642
GROUP OF NAH YUNG-SUK HATERS FORMED

1607
01:12:35,726 --> 01:12:38,687
He's my dear junior colleague too.

1608
01:12:38,771 --> 01:12:40,814
And we're all on the same team.

1609
01:12:40,898 --> 01:12:42,399
Hey, don't you hear

1610
01:12:42,483 --> 01:12:43,901
some kind of strange toilet sound?

1611
01:12:44,943 --> 01:12:46,362
PRODUCER NAH ON THE DEFENSIVE

1612
01:12:46,445 --> 01:12:47,279
No?

1613
01:12:48,280 --> 01:12:50,282
I should go take a dump.

1614
01:12:52,034 --> 01:12:53,577
Excuse me.

1615
01:12:53,660 --> 01:12:55,162
DOWOON LEAVES HIS SEAT FOR A MOMENT

1616
01:12:56,830 --> 01:12:58,040
QUIETLY

1617
01:12:58,582 --> 01:12:59,583
Excuse me, Car-the.

1618
01:12:59,666 --> 01:13:02,086
I bought these <i>mandu</i>
while thinking of you.

1619
01:13:03,462 --> 01:13:05,214
You can have these all by yourself.

1620
01:13:05,798 --> 01:13:07,341
You want to drive us further away?

1621
01:13:07,424 --> 01:13:08,467
WHAT IS HAPPENING?

1622
01:13:08,550 --> 01:13:10,010
It's because he likes <i>mandu.</i>

1623
01:13:10,094 --> 01:13:11,053
I thought of him.

1624
01:13:11,136 --> 01:13:11,970
VERY SUSPICIOUS

1625
01:13:12,054 --> 01:13:13,555
Don't let it slide like this…

1626
01:13:14,181 --> 01:13:15,057
If you do…

1627
01:13:15,140 --> 01:13:16,308
What kind of <i>mandu</i> are these?

1628
01:13:16,392 --> 01:13:17,559
MANDU ALREADY ACCEPTED

1629
01:13:18,811 --> 01:13:20,938
I put a little something
in with the <i>mandu.</i>

1630
01:13:22,815 --> 01:13:24,149
I got 5 km with the <i>mandu.</i>

1631
01:13:26,193 --> 01:13:27,069
ACCUMULATED KM BADGES

1632
01:13:27,152 --> 01:13:28,237
I'm fine,

1633
01:13:28,320 --> 01:13:30,030
but I don't know about Chae-min.

1634
01:13:30,739 --> 01:13:32,282
There was a father-like figure

1635
01:13:32,366 --> 01:13:34,785
who always watched
with gentle eyes from behind us.

1636
01:13:34,868 --> 01:13:36,662
All I can say is that he abandoned us.

1637
01:13:36,745 --> 01:13:37,913
You're right.

1638
01:13:39,373 --> 01:13:41,166
Chae-min, you look thirsty though.

1639
01:13:41,250 --> 01:13:42,126
Take a cup of Coke.

1640
01:13:42,209 --> 01:13:43,419
PRODUCER NAH HANDS HIM COKE

1641
01:13:43,502 --> 01:13:44,586
Chae-min doesn't like Coke.

1642
01:13:44,670 --> 01:13:45,921
It's good Coke. Have a sip.

1643
01:13:46,004 --> 01:13:48,090
-I only drink Sprite.
-Chae-min only drinks Sprite.

1644
01:13:48,173 --> 01:13:50,050
There are two cups. How strange.

1645
01:13:50,801 --> 01:13:53,053
LAUGHING

1646
01:13:53,137 --> 01:13:55,180
Chae-min, I'm asking just in case.

1647
01:13:55,264 --> 01:13:57,516
How do you feel about me
not going with you today?

1648
01:13:58,851 --> 01:13:59,685
What?

1649
01:14:00,602 --> 01:14:01,895
GRINNING FROM EAR TO EAR

1650
01:14:01,979 --> 01:14:03,981
I'm sure Producer Nah
didn't do it intentionally.

1651
01:14:04,064 --> 01:14:05,858
-Jung-won…
-You should stop too.

1652
01:14:05,941 --> 01:14:07,443
-You little brat.
-I want to join too.

1653
01:14:07,526 --> 01:14:10,446
That does it, Producer Nah!

1654
01:14:10,529 --> 01:14:12,614
CHAOS

1655
01:14:12,698 --> 01:14:13,532
ONLY ONE LEFT OUT

1656
01:14:13,615 --> 01:14:14,867
He has his reasons, you know!

1657
01:14:14,950 --> 01:14:16,994
Producer Nah, this won't do!

1658
01:14:17,619 --> 01:14:19,830
I believe you should have
respect for elders.

1659
01:14:19,913 --> 01:14:21,582
Of course, up to this point…

1660
01:14:21,665 --> 01:14:22,833
Look at him.

1661
01:14:22,916 --> 01:14:24,793
I acted too rudely
to someone older than me.

1662
01:14:24,877 --> 01:14:25,961
Yeah, watch your emotions.

1663
01:14:26,044 --> 01:14:27,129
Well…

1664
01:14:29,798 --> 01:14:31,383
CHECKS RIGHT AWAY

1665
01:14:31,467 --> 01:14:32,301
Goodness.

1666
01:14:32,384 --> 01:14:33,218
Father.

1667
01:14:34,511 --> 01:14:35,846
How was your meal?

1668
01:14:36,346 --> 01:14:37,181
Yeah.

1669
01:14:37,264 --> 01:14:39,016
We're not strangers with Producer Nah.

1670
01:14:39,099 --> 01:14:41,518
ACCUMULATED KM BADGES

1671
01:14:41,602 --> 01:14:43,812
No, I apologize for my stomach.

1672
01:14:43,896 --> 01:14:46,023
-No!
-I apologize.

1673
01:14:46,106 --> 01:14:46,940
Come on.

1674
01:14:47,024 --> 01:14:48,442
Let's not argue over this.

1675
01:14:48,525 --> 01:14:50,360
No, I'm sorry. Chae-min.

1676
01:14:50,444 --> 01:14:52,112
I mean, how can you hike if you're sick?

1677
01:14:52,196 --> 01:14:53,280
Gosh, I'm tearing up.

1678
01:14:53,363 --> 01:14:55,032
TEARY-EYED

1679
01:14:55,115 --> 01:14:55,991
Thank you so much.

1680
01:14:56,950 --> 01:14:57,784
Seriously…

1681
01:14:58,535 --> 01:14:59,912
I'm so sorry.

1682
01:14:59,995 --> 01:15:02,122
-I didn't mean to do this.
-I'll go back up.

1683
01:15:02,206 --> 01:15:03,457
No.

1684
01:15:03,540 --> 01:15:05,000
-You don't have to.
-Come, now.

1685
01:15:05,667 --> 01:15:07,836
We only care about your health, Father.

1686
01:15:07,920 --> 01:15:11,048
-Then, we'll all forget about it.
-Yes.

1687
01:15:11,131 --> 01:15:13,133
THEY COME TO A DRAMATIC AGREEMENT

1688
01:15:13,217 --> 01:15:14,968
Congratulations on climbing
the three peaks.

1689
01:15:15,052 --> 01:15:16,011
Gosh.

1690
01:15:16,094 --> 01:15:17,763
I was just worried, you know.

1691
01:15:17,846 --> 01:15:19,973
Well, I felt really bad about it.

1692
01:15:20,057 --> 01:15:22,184
When we were criticizing you earlier,
we felt bad.

1693
01:15:22,267 --> 01:15:23,143
You know, right?

1694
01:15:23,227 --> 01:15:25,479
Of course, I felt it, but…

1695
01:15:25,562 --> 01:15:27,481
You don't hate
Producer Nah that much, right?

1696
01:15:27,564 --> 01:15:28,649
DOWOON RETURNS WITH NO IDEA

1697
01:15:28,732 --> 01:15:29,942
-Right?
-Well, what can you do?

1698
01:15:30,442 --> 01:15:32,486
We all made up like grown men.

1699
01:15:32,569 --> 01:15:33,403
I see.

1700
01:15:33,487 --> 01:15:35,197
We were dragging it out for too long.

1701
01:15:35,280 --> 01:15:37,199
Yeah, you shouldn't hate people too much.

1702
01:15:37,282 --> 01:15:39,826
HOLDS NO GRUDGES

1703
01:15:39,910 --> 01:15:40,786
ACCUMULATED KM BADGES

1704
01:15:40,869 --> 01:15:42,538
I didn't think this would be so exciting.

1705
01:15:42,621 --> 01:15:43,872
TIME FOR YEONGNAM ALPS BADGES

1706
01:15:43,956 --> 01:15:45,123
You're excited?

1707
01:15:46,625 --> 01:15:49,461
The Yeongnam Alps' three-peak challenge.

1708
01:15:51,129 --> 01:15:51,964
Congratulations.

1709
01:15:52,047 --> 01:15:53,048
QUEST COMPLETION BADGES

1710
01:15:53,131 --> 01:15:53,966
How many km is it?

1711
01:15:54,049 --> 01:15:54,883
Thank you.

1712
01:15:56,677 --> 01:15:57,719
Your commemorative badges.

1713
01:15:58,303 --> 01:16:00,180
I'm guessing it should be 16 or 17 km?

1714
01:16:00,264 --> 01:16:01,598
PEAK 1

1715
01:16:01,682 --> 01:16:03,058
GANWOLSAN

1716
01:16:03,141 --> 01:16:04,476
SINBULSAN

1717
01:16:04,560 --> 01:16:06,436
PEAK 2

1718
01:16:07,563 --> 01:16:08,772
YEONGCHUKSAN

1719
01:16:08,855 --> 01:16:10,315
PEAK 3

1720
01:16:11,400 --> 01:16:13,652
<i>You have earned 16 km per person.</i>

1721
01:16:13,735 --> 01:16:15,946
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3 PEAKS
16 KM ROUND TRIP

1722
01:16:16,530 --> 01:16:19,074
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3 PEAKS

1723
01:16:19,157 --> 01:16:21,243
We said we'd give you something
if you passed 50 km.

1724
01:16:21,326 --> 01:16:24,663
-Gold.
-Gold worth three million won.

1725
01:16:25,497 --> 01:16:27,124
We made them with 15 g of gold.

1726
01:16:27,207 --> 01:16:28,500
-You did?
-We each get 3.75 g?

1727
01:16:28,584 --> 01:16:30,711
Each person will get 3.75 g.

1728
01:16:30,794 --> 01:16:31,837
They're gold badges.

1729
01:16:31,920 --> 01:16:32,963
You're really giving them?

1730
01:16:33,046 --> 01:16:34,840
PURE GOLD
3.75 G

1731
01:16:34,923 --> 01:16:36,842
WE'RE REALLY GIVING THEM TO YOU

1732
01:16:36,925 --> 01:16:40,012
I'll announce the total accumulated km
for each of you.

1733
01:16:40,095 --> 01:16:41,013
Car, the garden.

1734
01:16:41,722 --> 01:16:42,639
Yes?

1735
01:16:42,723 --> 01:16:43,724
Car, the garden.

1736
01:16:44,558 --> 01:16:45,851
You've earned 60 km.

1737
01:16:47,686 --> 01:16:51,189
5 KM FROM SECRET DEAL

1738
01:16:52,482 --> 01:16:53,317
GENTLE

1739
01:16:53,400 --> 01:16:54,651
Tell us how you feel.

1740
01:16:55,319 --> 01:16:56,528
"The Mountain and Me."

1741
01:16:57,446 --> 01:16:59,323
EMOTIONAL THOUGHTS BEFITTING
A BALLAD SINGER

1742
01:16:59,406 --> 01:17:00,699
"The Mountain and Me."

1743
01:17:01,366 --> 01:17:04,536
In this world comprised of only these two,

1744
01:17:05,454 --> 01:17:07,414
I, the singer Car, the garden,

1745
01:17:08,665 --> 01:17:11,001
promise to become someone

1746
01:17:11,084 --> 01:17:13,170
who will walk side by side
with the mountains.

1747
01:17:13,253 --> 01:17:16,006
ENJOYING A GOOD SHOW

1748
01:17:16,089 --> 01:17:16,923
Next.

1749
01:17:17,758 --> 01:17:19,343
It's our Minister of Foreign Affairs.

1750
01:17:19,426 --> 01:17:20,510
Lee Chae-min.

1751
01:17:21,136 --> 01:17:22,346
You've earned 60 km.

1752
01:17:24,640 --> 01:17:27,059
5 KM FROM SECRET DEAL

1753
01:17:27,142 --> 01:17:28,810
Please give us a few words, Minister.

1754
01:17:28,894 --> 01:17:30,395
At this young age…

1755
01:17:31,146 --> 01:17:32,773
LEE CHAE-MIN, AGE 27

1756
01:17:32,856 --> 01:17:37,527
…I managed to cover
a long distance of 60 km.

1757
01:17:38,528 --> 01:17:40,322
I first would like to thank my father.

1758
01:17:42,491 --> 01:17:43,367
With…

1759
01:17:44,117 --> 01:17:47,412
With this opportunity you gave me,
I was able to learn about life.

1760
01:17:47,496 --> 01:17:48,705
Since I've come this far,

1761
01:17:48,789 --> 01:17:52,084
I thought about achieving 100 km

1762
01:17:52,167 --> 01:17:53,502
for a moment.

1763
01:17:53,585 --> 01:17:57,172
But it's not something that can happen
based solely on what I think.

1764
01:17:57,255 --> 01:18:00,634
ONE PERSON IS ESPECIALLY SHOCKED

1765
01:18:00,717 --> 01:18:04,012
I'll quietly and diligently try my best.

1766
01:18:04,096 --> 01:18:04,930
Thank you.

1767
01:18:05,013 --> 01:18:07,057
PRODUCTION-FRIENDLY
MINISTER OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS

1768
01:18:07,140 --> 01:18:08,308
Anyway, you two earned 60 km.

1769
01:18:08,392 --> 01:18:10,060
THE SEONGPANAK TEAM FINISH THEIR REMARKS

1770
01:18:10,143 --> 01:18:11,436
Next, Tarzzan.

1771
01:18:11,520 --> 01:18:12,354
The president.

1772
01:18:12,938 --> 01:18:15,065
You've earned 59 km.

1773
01:18:16,108 --> 01:18:17,776
5 KM FROM SECRET DEAL

1774
01:18:17,859 --> 01:18:19,361
President Tar, tell us how you feel.

1775
01:18:19,444 --> 01:18:21,321
As the president of Descend Club,

1776
01:18:21,405 --> 01:18:23,782
it's been an honor to climb

1777
01:18:23,865 --> 01:18:26,535
incredible mountains
with such good members.

1778
01:18:26,618 --> 01:18:28,286
And my name is Tarzzan.

1779
01:18:28,912 --> 01:18:31,832
When you mention "Tarzzan,"
you think of mountains, and vice-versa.

1780
01:18:33,083 --> 01:18:34,835
I'll make sure we reach 100 km.

1781
01:18:36,253 --> 01:18:37,087
Everyone is…

1782
01:18:39,965 --> 01:18:41,007
We should talk about it.

1783
01:18:42,592 --> 01:18:46,096
I promise to be a president
who listens to his fellow members.

1784
01:18:48,014 --> 01:18:50,350
So, Tarzzan earned 59 km.

1785
01:18:50,434 --> 01:18:53,103
Lastly, the Minister of Transport.

1786
01:18:53,186 --> 01:18:54,312
Dowoon.

1787
01:18:54,396 --> 01:18:56,606
You've earned 54 km.

1788
01:18:58,358 --> 01:19:00,652
What a shame.
Still, let's give him a hand.

1789
01:19:00,736 --> 01:19:01,570
Why?

1790
01:19:03,113 --> 01:19:03,947
But why?

1791
01:19:04,030 --> 01:19:04,865
BECAUSE…

1792
01:19:04,948 --> 01:19:07,701
HE HAD NO SECRET DEAL

1793
01:19:07,784 --> 01:19:10,203
-That's how the cookie crumbles.
-What you can do?

1794
01:19:10,287 --> 01:19:11,872
I'm sure they calculated accurately.

1795
01:19:11,955 --> 01:19:13,749
They wouldn't get the math wrong.

1796
01:19:13,832 --> 01:19:16,042
Shouldn't I be at 59 km too?

1797
01:19:16,126 --> 01:19:17,210
FRUSTRATED

1798
01:19:17,294 --> 01:19:18,754
BOGUS ARGUMENTS CONTINUES

1799
01:19:18,837 --> 01:19:20,881
Once you climb, the distances can differ.

1800
01:19:20,964 --> 01:19:22,549
That's nonsense.

1801
01:19:23,133 --> 01:19:25,343
Hey, this is ridiculous.

1802
01:19:26,094 --> 01:19:27,596
Something must've happened.

1803
01:19:28,180 --> 01:19:29,264
Something happened.

1804
01:19:29,347 --> 01:19:30,599
FEIGNING IGNORANCE

1805
01:19:30,682 --> 01:19:31,933
Tell us how you feel first.

1806
01:19:32,017 --> 01:19:34,436
-Tell us how you feel.
-54 km is amazing too.

1807
01:19:34,519 --> 01:19:36,146
I've only seen the ocean my whole life.

1808
01:19:36,813 --> 01:19:38,190
But I got the chance

1809
01:19:38,899 --> 01:19:41,151
to hike mountains

1810
01:19:41,943 --> 01:19:45,655
while surrounded
by such wonderful and famous members,

1811
01:19:45,739 --> 01:19:47,657
and that was really great.

1812
01:19:47,741 --> 01:19:49,868
I don't know how long we'll be together.

1813
01:19:49,951 --> 01:19:51,620
Come on! Don't try to run away again.

1814
01:19:51,703 --> 01:19:53,038
SOCIAL DISTANCING

1815
01:19:53,121 --> 01:19:55,123
I don't know how long we'll be together,

1816
01:19:55,207 --> 01:19:56,792
but I'll do my best until the end.

1817
01:19:59,544 --> 01:20:01,087
I'll hand out the gold badges now.

1818
01:20:01,171 --> 01:20:02,923
Hold on. Why am I at 54 km?

1819
01:20:03,799 --> 01:20:05,383
Please explain this to me.

1820
01:20:05,467 --> 01:20:09,137
That was according to our calculations.

1821
01:20:09,221 --> 01:20:10,597
But there could've been a mistake.

1822
01:20:10,680 --> 01:20:12,140
So, I'll ask the three of you.

1823
01:20:12,224 --> 01:20:14,559
Was our calculation of 54 km wrong?

1824
01:20:14,643 --> 01:20:15,769
There was no error.

1825
01:20:15,852 --> 01:20:16,686
Really?

1826
01:20:16,770 --> 01:20:17,604
It's true.

1827
01:20:17,687 --> 01:20:19,147
Car-the might think differently.

1828
01:20:19,231 --> 01:20:20,232
No, it's true.

1829
01:20:21,024 --> 01:20:24,152
You jerks made a deal while I was away!

1830
01:20:24,236 --> 01:20:26,822
I hurried my way down
and gave all of you rides!

1831
01:20:26,905 --> 01:20:28,031
-You little…
-Dowoon.

1832
01:20:28,114 --> 01:20:29,324
I thought highly of you!

1833
01:20:29,407 --> 01:20:30,367
FURIOUS

1834
01:20:30,450 --> 01:20:31,409
Hear me out.

1835
01:20:31,493 --> 01:20:32,786
What's there to make a deal for?

1836
01:20:32,869 --> 01:20:33,703
CALM DOWN

1837
01:20:33,787 --> 01:20:34,913
There's nothing.

1838
01:20:34,996 --> 01:20:37,666
This is their job.
They wouldn't make mistakes calculating.

1839
01:20:38,583 --> 01:20:39,417
He's right.

1840
01:20:39,501 --> 01:20:40,710
ALREADY FULL OF DISTRUST

1841
01:20:40,794 --> 01:20:42,754
You know, Dowoon,

1842
01:20:42,838 --> 01:20:44,923
I kept refusing to take it.

1843
01:20:45,632 --> 01:20:47,717
JUNG-WON…

1844
01:20:48,844 --> 01:20:51,304
You got extra km and kept your mouth shut.

1845
01:20:51,388 --> 01:20:53,306
But what about me?

1846
01:20:53,390 --> 01:20:54,474
Seriously.

1847
01:20:54,558 --> 01:20:57,477
You guys are some weird people.

1848
01:20:57,561 --> 01:21:00,522
I drove four hours to get here.

1849
01:21:01,398 --> 01:21:03,817
FEELING BETRAYED

1850
01:21:03,900 --> 01:21:07,445
Still, despite being your first time
hiking these mountains,

1851
01:21:07,529 --> 01:21:09,865
you have already hit 50 km.

1852
01:21:10,448 --> 01:21:11,283
GOLD BADGES AWARDED

1853
01:21:11,366 --> 01:21:13,118
Congratulations. They're real gold badges.

1854
01:21:16,329 --> 01:21:17,163
IMPRESSED

1855
01:21:20,584 --> 01:21:24,087
WHILE THEY EACH CHECK OUT
THEIR GOLD BADGES

1856
01:21:24,170 --> 01:21:25,255
Dowoon.

1857
01:21:25,338 --> 01:21:27,090
-Thank you so much for driving.
-Dowoon.

1858
01:21:27,757 --> 01:21:29,217
We put in something small too.

1859
01:21:29,301 --> 01:21:30,760
GOLD BADGE AWARDED SEPARATELY TO HIM

1860
01:21:32,012 --> 01:21:33,221
There we go.

1861
01:21:34,306 --> 01:21:36,641
DOWOON GETS AN EXTRA 5 KM TOO

1862
01:21:36,725 --> 01:21:38,643
It turns out they're good people.

1863
01:21:39,394 --> 01:21:41,104
ACCUMULATED KM BADGES

1864
01:21:41,187 --> 01:21:42,606
He takes responsibility.

1865
01:21:43,732 --> 01:21:45,775
You've worked so hard
on your quests so far.

1866
01:21:45,859 --> 01:21:48,069
Only the last quest remains.

1867
01:21:48,945 --> 01:21:50,530
We will reveal the final quest.

1868
01:21:50,614 --> 01:21:51,615
The final quest is…

1869
01:21:59,080 --> 01:22:00,415
Climbing this is the final quest.

1870
01:22:00,498 --> 01:22:01,625
-Yeah.
-Congratulations!

1871
01:22:01,708 --> 01:22:02,667
I saw it coming.

1872
01:22:02,751 --> 01:22:04,461
Yeah, I knew this would happen.

1873
01:22:04,544 --> 01:22:06,296
I was wondering why
it hadn't shown up yet.

1874
01:22:08,340 --> 01:22:10,675
FOR THE FIRST TIME ON TAKE A HIKE!

1875
01:22:12,761 --> 01:22:13,595
Let's not shoot it.

1876
01:22:15,221 --> 01:22:16,389
Yeah, that may be better.

1877
01:22:16,473 --> 01:22:17,766
It's dangerous here.

1878
01:22:17,849 --> 01:22:19,517
One, two, three.

1879
01:22:19,601 --> 01:22:21,937
THEY GIVE UP FILMING
HALFWAY INTO THE FINAL QUEST

1880
01:22:22,687 --> 01:22:24,898
It was a lot harder
than the other mountains.

1881
01:22:24,981 --> 01:22:25,815
It was a bit…

1882
01:22:34,407 --> 01:22:35,909
<i>I mean, what do you want me to do?</i>

1883
01:22:35,992 --> 01:22:37,911
<i>What do you want from me?</i>

1884
01:22:37,994 --> 01:22:39,829
That section had no mercy.

1885
01:22:39,913 --> 01:22:40,747
That place…

1886
01:22:45,210 --> 01:22:46,044
Geez!

1887
01:22:48,004 --> 01:22:49,547
This was the hardest one for me.

1888
01:22:50,215 --> 01:22:51,383
-Harder than Seoraksan?
-Yes.

1889
01:22:51,883 --> 01:22:53,051
I don't know why.

1890
01:22:53,885 --> 01:22:55,762
This place was the worst.

1891
01:22:57,514 --> 01:22:58,431
It was just…

1892
01:23:00,392 --> 01:23:02,227
No joke. This place is…

1893
01:23:02,310 --> 01:23:04,854
a ********.

1894
01:23:04,938 --> 01:23:09,109
Forget about hiking. It's a ********.

1895
01:23:09,192 --> 01:23:10,026
Seriously.

1896
01:23:10,652 --> 01:23:11,820
I have nothing else to say.

1897
01:23:11,903 --> 01:23:15,407
BEFORE THE FINAL QUEST

1898
01:23:15,490 --> 01:23:16,741
<i>-Jeotgal.</i>
-Wrong!

1899
01:23:16,825 --> 01:23:20,120
DESCEND CLUB'S SECOND ACTIVITY

1900
01:23:20,203 --> 01:23:21,621
Hotdog!

1901
01:23:21,705 --> 01:23:22,622
Bale.

1902
01:23:23,123 --> 01:23:23,957
Wrong!

1903
01:23:24,040 --> 01:23:25,125
THE SAME OLD KIM UI-HAN

1904
01:23:25,208 --> 01:23:26,584
-There's Santa Claus.
-Wrong!

1905
01:23:26,668 --> 01:23:27,669
AND ZZAN OF TAR

1906
01:23:27,752 --> 01:23:28,670
Hey, come on!

1907
01:23:28,753 --> 01:23:30,088
Three, two…

1908
01:23:30,171 --> 01:23:31,006
Gets bigger!

1909
01:23:31,089 --> 01:23:31,923
Wrong!

1910
01:23:33,633 --> 01:23:36,386
MINISTER OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS'
UNEXPECTED PERFORMANCE

1911
01:23:36,469 --> 01:23:40,432
Could you make sure to edit this?
I think it's going to look bad.

1912
01:23:41,725 --> 01:23:42,559
Correct!

1913
01:23:42,642 --> 01:23:45,562
THE LAST GAME WITH KM ON THE LINE

1914
01:23:45,645 --> 01:23:47,981
THE UNEXPECTED REBELLION OF DESCEND CLUB

1915
01:23:48,064 --> 01:23:49,149
We'll go home now!

1916
01:23:50,108 --> 01:23:50,942
Then, what happens?

1917
01:23:51,026 --> 01:23:52,444
CALCULATIONS GET COMPLICATED

1918
01:23:52,527 --> 01:23:54,195
It's been a while since I've gone all in.

1919
01:23:56,990 --> 01:23:58,033
We're over 100.

1920
01:23:58,116 --> 01:24:00,535
-We're over 100. We went over 100!
-Hold on!

1921
01:24:00,618 --> 01:24:01,745
We went over 100!

1922
01:24:01,828 --> 01:24:03,997
WHAT WILL BECOME OF DESCEND CLUB?

1923
01:24:04,080 --> 01:24:05,999
We went over 100.

1924
01:25:04,057 --> 01:25:06,059
Subtitle translation by: Kim Yeeun
